- Are you done dancing?
- Yes.

155
00:10:51.875 --> 00:10:53.792
- Are you happy now?
- Yes.

156
00:10:53.875 --> 00:10:55.675
- Can we go home now?
- No, first give me a hug.

157
00:10:55.708 --> 00:10:57.125
<i>It's time to party!</i>

158
00:10:59.042 --> 00:11:02.750
Hey, here comes the TV!

159
00:11:02.833 --> 00:11:05.208
Was he peddling like a turtle?

160
00:11:05.292 --> 00:11:07.000
It's almost 9:00 a.m., brother-in-law.

161
00:11:07.083 --> 00:11:09.000
- It's alright, sister-in-law.
- Here, give it.

162
00:11:09.083 --> 00:11:11.208
- Be careful.
- Don't just stand there, all of you!

163
00:11:11.292 --> 00:11:12.667
- Give him a hand.
- We're going.

164
00:11:12.750 --> 00:11:14.333
Please go and find Banke.

165
00:11:14.417 --> 00:11:16.177
- Banke! Bankelal!
- God knows where he's gone.

166
00:11:16.250 --> 00:11:17.643
Brother, the day I become
a government officer,

167
00:11:17.667 --> 00:11:20.208
- Bankelal!
- I'll buy a TV just like this one.

168
00:11:20.292 --> 00:11:21.125
Really?

169
00:11:21.250 --> 00:11:22.893
I don't see any signs of that coming true.

170
00:11:22.917 --> 00:11:25.143
Exams are around the corner,
and you're not focused on your studies.

171
00:11:25.167 --> 00:11:26.583
Let me make it very clear, Birju.

172
00:11:26.667 --> 00:11:28.958
You won't set foot in those mines,
and that's final.

173
00:11:29.250 --> 00:11:30.375
Oh, okay.

174
00:11:30.458 --> 00:11:33.375
We've hardly seen you since
your daughter arrived.

175
00:11:33.458 --> 00:11:36.042
Brother Daddan,
I've been complaining about that as well.

176
00:11:36.125 --> 00:11:38.167
Don't listen to her. It's not true.

177
00:11:38.250 --> 00:11:40.625
I want every inch of the bus covered
in flowers,

178
00:11:40.708 --> 00:11:43.375
so all of Raniganj feels like a bouquet.

179
00:11:43.458 --> 00:11:45.542
Goodness! You're sinning
on an auspicious day.

180
00:11:45.625 --> 00:11:47.417
- Have some fear!
- Gods drink too. Let's go.

181
00:11:47.500 --> 00:11:48.667
You are incorrigible.

182
00:11:49.042 --> 00:11:50.583
Why did you call me here, Banke?

183
00:11:51.625 --> 00:11:53.601
There are several varieties
of flowers here, Sunita.

184
00:11:53.625 --> 00:11:54.792
Pick the one you like.

185
00:11:55.792 --> 00:11:58.625
I'll know your feelings for me.

186
00:12:02.000 --> 00:12:04.875
Shakuni played a really
wicked move in the last act.

187
00:12:04.958 --> 00:12:07.000
- Let's go.
- The Pandavas' anonymous exile is bound

188
00:12:07.083 --> 00:12:08.542
to get exposed today.

189
00:12:10.250 --> 00:12:11.890
Why don't you just sit on my lap instead?

190
00:12:11.917 --> 00:12:12.917
Move!

191
00:12:12.958 --> 00:12:13.792
Listen, Sudama.

192
00:12:13.875 --> 00:12:16.292
- My son will sit here.
- Leave my spot.

193
00:12:16.375 --> 00:12:19.167
- This is unfair.
- Old man…

194
00:12:20.083 --> 00:12:21.542
How do you plan to watch Mahabharata

195
00:12:21.833 --> 00:12:23.542
if you don't carry your glasses?

196
00:12:23.625 --> 00:12:25.708
Attention! Attention!

197
00:12:25.917 --> 00:12:28.208
Everyone is informed,

198
00:12:28.292 --> 00:12:33.458
that the bus leaves at 10:00 a.m. tomorrow
for Rekha's wedding.

199
00:12:33.542 --> 00:12:34.833
Wonderful!

200
00:12:34.917 --> 00:12:35.792
Great!

201
00:12:35.875 --> 00:12:39.917
So, everyone, be on time
and grab your seats.

202
00:12:40.000 --> 00:12:41.125
- We will!
- Understood?

203
00:12:41.208 --> 00:12:43.417
So that we all reach Ramgarh on time

204
00:12:43.500 --> 00:12:48.167
and proceed with Rekha's marriage
at the auspicious time.

205
00:12:49.375 --> 00:12:50.750
That's great news!

206
00:12:50.958 --> 00:12:52.375
Congratulations!

207
00:12:55.083 --> 00:12:58.167
Priest, it's time to sound the conch.

208
00:13:15.125 --> 00:13:17.417
- This is where the cap lamps are charged.
- Really, Uncle?

209
00:13:24.333 --> 00:13:27.375
Sir, starting tomorrow, I would
prefer not to work the night shifts.

210
00:13:27.542 --> 00:13:28.702
Okay, I'll see what I can do.

211
00:13:29.167 --> 00:13:30.250
Hello, sir.

212
00:13:32.542 --> 00:13:34.022
Planning to do overtime even tonight?

213
00:13:34.125 --> 00:13:35.125
Yes.

214
00:13:35.375 --> 00:13:37.917
Are you done making arrangements
for Rekha's wedding?

215
00:13:38.000 --> 00:13:40.000
Yes, I did.

216
00:13:55.958 --> 00:13:57.875
- Wait. Let me open it.
- Let them pass.

217
00:13:57.958 --> 00:13:58.792
Come on.

218
00:13:58.875 --> 00:14:01.542
Hurry up, guys.
The next shift is here.

219
00:14:01.750 --> 00:14:02.917
- Move ahead.
- Go, go.

220
00:14:03.208 --> 00:14:04.649
- Careful.
- Keep moving, Ram Khilawan.

221
00:14:06.125 --> 00:14:07.000
Hey, Pashu!

222
00:14:07.083 --> 00:14:08.125
- Uncle.
- Yes?

223
00:14:08.208 --> 00:14:09.458
It's too heavy.

224
00:14:09.542 --> 00:14:10.667
Get used to it. Move.

225
00:14:13.125 --> 00:14:14.605
You aren't carrying any booze, right?

226
00:14:14.708 --> 00:14:15.708
No.

227
00:14:15.792 --> 00:14:17.375
- Wait. Stop.
- Wait. What is this?

228
00:14:20.458 --> 00:14:21.833
Well, Tiger…

229
00:14:22.667 --> 00:14:24.708
see you in the morning!

230
00:14:50.667 --> 00:14:52.292
- Go, go, go.
- Push harder.

231
00:15:09.458 --> 00:15:10.458
Come on.

232
00:15:19.125 --> 00:15:20.143
Uncle, how much longer till we get there?

233
00:15:20.167 --> 00:15:21.809
- How much have you had to drink?
- I've knocked back three already.

234
00:15:21.833 --> 00:15:24.167
My son-in-law landed a government job.

235
00:15:24.250 --> 00:15:25.583
How much dowry is he demanding?

236
00:15:47.792 --> 00:15:48.875
You have it good.

237
00:15:48.958 --> 00:15:51.917
No matter what, you'll do as you please!

238
00:16:02.417 --> 00:16:04.583
Attention!

239
00:16:05.083 --> 00:16:07.708
Be alert!

240
00:16:08.417 --> 00:16:11.542
- Blast in progress!
- Blast?

241
00:16:11.625 --> 00:16:13.458
Be alert!

242
00:16:14.167 --> 00:16:16.292
Attention!

243
00:16:17.208 --> 00:16:19.458
Be alert!

244
00:16:24.875 --> 00:16:27.042
We've dug up a lot of coal today.

245
00:16:27.542 --> 00:16:29.833
Nice, that means we'll hit our target.

246
00:16:31.083 --> 00:16:33.167
- Make sure to check over there as well.
- On it, sir.

247
00:16:35.083 --> 00:16:37.833
- Speed it up, Daddan.
- I'm going.

248
00:16:40.333 --> 00:16:41.333
Check here as well.

249
00:16:46.542 --> 00:16:47.542
Water?

250
00:17:02.250 --> 00:17:03.500
Chasnala?

251
00:17:03.750 --> 00:17:06.375
Run!

252
00:17:09.125 --> 00:17:10.684
Yeah, which section are
you speaking from?

253
00:17:10.708 --> 00:17:12.708
Brother, water has entered the court line!

254
00:17:12.792 --> 00:17:13.792
What?

255
00:17:14.625 --> 00:17:17.083
Brother, the mines are flooding.

256
00:17:17.167 --> 00:17:18.167
Flooding?

257
00:17:18.875 --> 00:17:19.875
Good God.

258
00:17:20.250 --> 00:17:22.333
Run!

259
00:17:24.792 --> 00:17:26.125
- Get out of here!
- Get out!

260
00:17:38.500 --> 00:17:40.542
Don't stop, keep running!

261
00:18:11.875 --> 00:18:13.208
Run!

262
00:18:13.292 --> 00:18:14.917
Some of you rush towards pit two.

263
00:18:15.000 --> 00:18:17.083
The rest of you head towards pit one.

264
00:18:17.167 --> 00:18:18.750
Run!

265
00:20:12.042 --> 00:20:13.667
Brother, what happened?

266
00:20:14.208 --> 00:20:16.625
Flooding at Mahabir Colliery.

267
00:20:17.167 --> 00:20:19.375
Miners are trapped.
That's where I am headed.

268
00:20:21.083 --> 00:20:22.667
If only I could get out of this!

269
00:20:26.208 --> 00:20:27.250
- Diwakar!
- Yes, sir.

270
00:20:27.333 --> 00:20:29.393
Move the car quickly.
Need to get the rescue van out.

271
00:20:29.417 --> 00:20:30.250
Okay, sir.

272
00:20:30.333 --> 00:20:32.208
Come on. Move your car.

273
00:20:32.833 --> 00:20:33.833
Come on, move!

274
00:20:34.167 --> 00:20:36.667
- Move!
- Come on! Hurry!

275
00:20:36.750 --> 00:20:38.375
Come on. Push harder.

276
00:20:39.500 --> 00:20:41.000
- Hey!
- Bravo!

277
00:20:41.417 --> 00:20:43.250
- Push harder.
- Come on!

278
00:20:43.333 --> 00:20:45.458
Hurry. Push harder.

279
00:20:46.750 --> 00:20:48.250
- Stop. Stop.
- Please hurry!

280
00:20:48.333 --> 00:20:50.208
Move your truck quickly. Hurry up.

281
00:20:53.042 --> 00:20:55.042
Push it. Keep going.

282
00:20:59.083 --> 00:21:00.167
Hurry up.

283
00:21:00.458 --> 00:21:01.458
Good, keep it moving.

284
00:21:01.958 --> 00:21:03.292
Let them pass.

285
00:21:08.250 --> 00:21:09.375
- Diwakar.
- Yes, sir?

286
00:21:09.458 --> 00:21:11.219
Go back to the office
and inform the director

287
00:21:11.250 --> 00:21:12.708
that I am going to Mahabir. Okay?

288
00:21:12.958 --> 00:21:13.958
Okay, sir.

289
00:21:27.792 --> 00:21:29.167
We need an answer!

290
00:21:30.958 --> 00:21:32.542
Let us go!

291
00:21:32.625 --> 00:21:34.500
- Let us in!
- Move back!

292
00:21:36.875 --> 00:21:37.917
Move back!

293
00:21:39.667 --> 00:21:41.292
- Let us go!
- Open the gate!

294
00:21:48.167 --> 00:21:50.417
Where do you think you're going?

295
00:21:50.500 --> 00:21:51.625
Let me go!

296
00:21:52.000 --> 00:21:53.417
My husband is trapped down there!

297
00:21:53.500 --> 00:21:54.583
Leave me!

298
00:21:54.667 --> 00:21:56.083
I want to meet your boss.

299
00:22:11.208 --> 00:22:13.708
Shut down Coal India!

300
00:22:13.792 --> 00:22:15.500
Shut down Coal India!

301
00:22:15.583 --> 00:22:18.958
You knew that place was dangerous.
Why did you go there?

302
00:22:19.542 --> 00:22:20.833
Let us go in once.

303
00:22:20.917 --> 00:22:22.917
Who is responsible for this tragedy?

304
00:22:23.333 --> 00:22:25.333
Is my brother alright?

305
00:22:25.417 --> 00:22:27.375
Move back!

306
00:22:27.458 --> 00:22:29.042
Why should we move back?

307
00:22:29.125 --> 00:22:32.833
If that Bansi,
Devi's husband, made it out,

308
00:22:32.917 --> 00:22:34.875
why is my husband still trapped inside?

309
00:22:35.333 --> 00:22:39.250
Let me go in or call your boss!

310
00:22:39.333 --> 00:22:41.042
Have you lost your mind?
Stay back.

311
00:22:41.125 --> 00:22:43.583
Hey… calm down!

312
00:22:44.917 --> 00:22:47.757
When the man of the house is missing,
the family is bound to be enraged.

313
00:22:48.208 --> 00:22:51.625
- I've been trying to explain...
- Now is not the time to give explanations.

314
00:22:52.750 --> 00:22:54.125
It's time to understand them.

315
00:22:54.542 --> 00:22:55.542
Right?

316
00:22:58.542 --> 00:22:59.542
Sorry, sir.

317
00:23:02.667 --> 00:23:03.708
Sir.

318
00:23:04.333 --> 00:23:07.000
No one's telling us
what condition they are in.

319
00:23:07.375 --> 00:23:09.208
Please help us, sir.

320
00:23:09.417 --> 00:23:11.250
Everyone's making excuses.

321
00:23:11.333 --> 00:23:14.417
- No one's listening to us.
- Tell us, sir.

322
00:23:14.958 --> 00:23:15.958
Sir…

323
00:23:16.958 --> 00:23:18.792
please tell us.

324
00:23:19.083 --> 00:23:22.250
When will Banke
and my brother-in-law come out, sir?

325
00:23:22.333 --> 00:23:23.333
Very soon.

326
00:23:23.500 --> 00:23:24.940
I assure you everyone will come out.

327
00:23:26.208 --> 00:23:29.000
The management
is taking every possible measure.

328
00:23:29.250 --> 00:23:30.250
Measures?

329
00:23:30.958 --> 00:23:32.042
What measures?

330
00:23:32.958 --> 00:23:34.000
You have to find them.

331
00:23:34.958 --> 00:23:38.333
I lost my brother in the Chasnala mines.

332
00:23:39.500 --> 00:23:42.000
And now, I can't…

333
00:23:43.708 --> 00:23:44.708
- Sister-in-law!
- Durga.

334
00:23:45.583 --> 00:23:46.708
- Sister-in-law!
- Durga.

335
00:23:48.875 --> 00:23:51.292
- What's wrong?
- What is wrong with her?

336
00:23:51.792 --> 00:23:55.000
Sir! You can't hide your face like this.

337
00:23:55.250 --> 00:23:57.542
You don't have any answers, do you?

338
00:23:57.917 --> 00:24:00.375
We cannot fall weak, Durga.

339
00:24:00.458 --> 00:24:02.083
- Get some water!
- Mother!

340
00:24:02.667 --> 00:24:04.042
Is my father alright?

341
00:24:06.042 --> 00:24:08.792
Everyone's misleading us.

342
00:24:08.875 --> 00:24:11.750
Move aside, everyone.
Let her get some fresh air.

343
00:24:13.458 --> 00:24:14.458
Hold this.

344
00:24:16.667 --> 00:24:17.667
Listen, child.

345
00:24:18.375 --> 00:24:19.375
Rub her hands.

346
00:24:36.667 --> 00:24:38.292
Drink this water.

347
00:24:38.792 --> 00:24:39.792
Drink it.

348
00:24:40.750 --> 00:24:41.750
Easy.

349
00:24:46.375 --> 00:24:48.667
Firstly, stop being negative.

350
00:24:49.500 --> 00:24:51.875
Right now, you need to be brave

351
00:24:52.167 --> 00:24:53.917
and have faith in the management.

352
00:24:55.208 --> 00:24:59.167
<i>Ujjwal sir is surely looking for
a solution to save the men.</i>

353
00:25:00.083 --> 00:25:01.583
<i>No one is hiding.</i>

354
00:25:02.583 --> 00:25:04.042
<i>We are one family.</i>

355
00:25:05.125 --> 00:25:09.208
<i>We should stand together
in such tough times. Okay?</i>

356
00:25:09.875 --> 00:25:12.042
<i>Soon you will all be informed.</i>

357
00:25:12.708 --> 00:25:15.000
<i>Don't worry.
Everything will be okay.</i>

358
00:25:21.583 --> 00:25:23.583
Kasim. Who is he?

359
00:25:25.417 --> 00:25:26.458
Ujjwal sir and this guy

360
00:25:26.667 --> 00:25:28.875
used to work together
in the coal mines of England.

361
00:25:29.083 --> 00:25:30.625
He was in Durgapur for a conference.

362
00:25:30.708 --> 00:25:32.708
Ujjwal sir has called him for advice.

363
00:25:39.042 --> 00:25:41.583
Mr. Ujjwal,
I don't think they could be alive.

364
00:25:42.333 --> 00:25:44.208
There'll be just dead bodies
down there now.

365
00:25:47.583 --> 00:25:48.583
Let's go.

366
00:25:52.083 --> 00:25:53.083
Sir…

367
00:25:53.625 --> 00:25:56.208
- the villagers are getting violent.
- It's not safe to be here.

368
00:25:56.292 --> 00:25:57.892
The car's waiting at the back door, sir.

369
00:25:59.958 --> 00:26:01.583
Do you have any rescue plans?

370
00:26:01.750 --> 00:26:02.750
Of course, sir.

371
00:26:02.833 --> 00:26:05.000
As soon as we find a way
to get down there,

372
00:26:05.083 --> 00:26:06.833
according to DGMS rules,

373
00:26:06.917 --> 00:26:10.625
I'll take four men with stretchers,
and rescue the trapped miners.

374
00:26:11.167 --> 00:26:12.417
You call that a solution, Basu?

375
00:26:12.500 --> 00:26:16.042
Sir, such accidents occur
when safety rules are ignored.

376
00:26:16.125 --> 00:26:17.542
I had warned Kasim about the risks.

377
00:26:17.750 --> 00:26:18.667
But he said…

378
00:26:18.750 --> 00:26:20.768
"Why do you enter the mines
if you're afraid of taking risks?"

379
00:26:20.792 --> 00:26:22.500
Hey… when did you tell me?

380
00:26:22.583 --> 00:26:24.042
- I did.
- You must've told him.

381
00:26:24.125 --> 00:26:26.625
- Listen...
- This is not the time to blame each other.

382
00:26:27.875 --> 00:26:30.333
We need to rectify our mistakes.

383
00:26:32.250 --> 00:26:35.375
Sir, the families outside
want to know what our next step is.

384
00:26:35.708 --> 00:26:36.750
Who is he, Ujjwal?

385
00:26:39.250 --> 00:26:40.375
This is Jaswant Singh Gill.

386
00:26:41.125 --> 00:26:43.917
GM of SP Mines
and a rescue-trained officer.

387
00:26:46.042 --> 00:26:47.417
Sir, can I be of any help?

388
00:26:52.917 --> 00:26:54.184
It was a relief to see you here.

389
00:26:54.208 --> 00:26:55.875
But how did you learn about the accident?

390
00:26:55.958 --> 00:26:57.375
Superintendent Basu told me.

391
00:26:58.625 --> 00:27:01.083
Thank God you are here!

392
00:27:01.375 --> 00:27:03.792
There's a lot of negativity around.

393
00:27:03.875 --> 00:27:04.958
I am totally numb.

394
00:27:05.042 --> 00:27:06.750
I am completely alone.

395
00:27:07.417 --> 00:27:08.583
I really needed you, Gill

396
00:27:09.292 --> 00:27:10.292
Don't worry, sir.

397
00:27:10.542 --> 00:27:11.667
We will overcome this.

398
00:27:11.750 --> 00:27:12.750
Thank you.

399
00:27:21.958 --> 00:27:23.000
Brief me quickly.

400
00:27:23.375 --> 00:27:25.042
Sir, this is the Mahabir Colliery.

401
00:27:25.125 --> 00:27:26.375
At a depth of 350 feet

402
00:27:26.458 --> 00:27:28.434
is the Narayankuri seam
spread over an area of five kilometers,

403
00:27:28.458 --> 00:27:31.917
where 232 miners were working overtime
during the 12:00 a.m. shift.

404
00:27:32.000 --> 00:27:33.875
The work was done in three sections.

405
00:27:33.958 --> 00:27:35.625
Mining was under "Behra"…

406
00:27:36.208 --> 00:27:37.208
Anant Pandey.

407
00:27:37.583 --> 00:27:38.792
He's hard of hearing, sir.

408
00:27:40.917 --> 00:27:43.726
Sixty-five miners under Behra were
working here, under the railway line.

409
00:27:43.750 --> 00:27:45.792
- Hey!
- Start drilling.

410
00:27:45.875 --> 00:27:47.375
Shaligram, Noor, and Bankelal

411
00:27:47.458 --> 00:27:49.339
<i>were doing maintenance work
in the trolley area.</i>

412
00:27:52.208 --> 00:27:54.089
Forty-two miners were moving
the coal from here.

413
00:27:54.750 --> 00:27:57.000
<i>At the highway line, under Lakhan.</i>

414
00:27:58.167 --> 00:28:00.375
And here,
ninety-four of Daddan's miners

415
00:28:00.458 --> 00:28:01.699
were working in the court line.

416
00:28:02.125 --> 00:28:03.518
Which section did the blast go off?

417
00:28:03.542 --> 00:28:04.542
In Daddan's section.

418
00:28:06.167 --> 00:28:07.601
Sir, under the pressure of production,

419
00:28:07.625 --> 00:28:10.958
management crossed
this 60-meter danger strip

420
00:28:11.042 --> 00:28:12.042
and blasted this space.

421
00:28:12.708 --> 00:28:14.667
This ceiling was connected
to the Ningha pit,

422
00:28:14.750 --> 00:28:16.101
which had been closed for 70 years,

423
00:28:16.125 --> 00:28:19.083
and had ten trillion gallons
of water at the least.

424
00:28:20.500 --> 00:28:23.792
And this water is quickly seeping
into the Narayankuri seam.

425
00:28:27.542 --> 00:28:30.958
After Daddan's alert,
which section did you call first?

426
00:28:31.042 --> 00:28:32.042
Behra's section.

427
00:28:32.292 --> 00:28:35.750
<i>Sir, no one answered the phone.</i>

428
00:28:38.042 --> 00:28:40.322
<i>- Then what did you do?
- I quickly called the highway line.</i>

429
00:28:40.833 --> 00:28:42.167
Get out of there immediately.

430
00:28:42.250 --> 00:28:44.090
The court line is flooded.
Water is seeping in.

431
00:28:44.125 --> 00:28:45.917
The mines are flooding! Run!

432
00:28:49.167 --> 00:28:51.167
- Then?
- I called Behra again.

433
00:28:52.583 --> 00:28:53.583
Pick up, Behra!

434
00:28:56.667 --> 00:28:58.125
And Pandey didn't pick up again?

435
00:28:58.208 --> 00:28:59.625
Gop answered the phone.

436
00:28:59.708 --> 00:29:00.829
But nearly 20 minutes later.

437
00:29:01.875 --> 00:29:03.458
- Yes?
- Gop, run.

438
00:29:03.708 --> 00:29:05.643
The court line's flooding!
Water's getting seeping in!

439
00:29:05.667 --> 00:29:07.750
Hey! Listen…

440
00:29:08.000 --> 00:29:10.875
- Gop!
- Run for your lives, everyone!

441
00:29:10.958 --> 00:29:12.292
The mines are flooding!

442
00:29:19.125 --> 00:29:20.458
Run fast, Behra!

443
00:29:21.042 --> 00:29:23.208
You mean to say
they never made it to Chanak?

444
00:29:23.292 --> 00:29:24.125
Yes, sir.

445
00:29:24.208 --> 00:29:28.750
I was the last one to make it out.
But I didn't see Behra or his men.

446
00:29:28.833 --> 00:29:30.375
But I did see the water coming.

447
00:29:35.292 --> 00:29:37.583
Pull!

448
00:29:37.958 --> 00:29:42.583
I can see the water coming!
Pull now!

449
00:29:53.542 --> 00:29:55.250
Any contact with the missing miners?

450
00:29:55.333 --> 00:29:58.208
After speaking to Gop,
the CDS system failed as well.

451
00:29:58.375 --> 00:30:00.833
- How many miners made it out?
- 161 miners.

452
00:30:00.917 --> 00:30:03.500
So, 71 miners are still missing. Right?

453
00:30:03.583 --> 00:30:04.500
- Yes.
- Six from the highway line,

454
00:30:04.583 --> 00:30:06.667
and all sixty-five miners
from Behra's section.

455
00:30:07.542 --> 00:30:08.542
Have a look, sir.

456
00:30:12.958 --> 00:30:14.199
What do these crosses indicate?

457
00:30:14.458 --> 00:30:15.458
Dead.

458
00:30:18.792 --> 00:30:19.792
Sir…

459
00:30:20.417 --> 00:30:22.833
they must have tried to get to Chanak.

460
00:30:23.583 --> 00:30:25.167
The water must have swept them away.

461
00:30:25.417 --> 00:30:26.417
Ujjwal…

462
00:30:27.083 --> 00:30:28.625
I also assume all are dead.

463
00:30:32.958 --> 00:30:33.958
Sir…

464
00:30:34.167 --> 00:30:37.042
with due regard,
assumption is not a solution.

465
00:30:37.167 --> 00:30:39.083
No one saw them die.

466
00:30:39.167 --> 00:30:41.667
And no one knows if they are alive.

467
00:30:41.958 --> 00:30:44.000
The chances of survival are fifty-fifty.

468
00:30:44.708 --> 00:30:47.375
Sir, we should hope they are alive.

469
00:30:47.750 --> 00:30:50.833
Because if there is a single
life breathing down there,

470
00:30:51.167 --> 00:30:52.708
he's probably waiting for us.

471
00:30:53.417 --> 00:30:54.708
Who is the survey officer?

472
00:30:55.042 --> 00:30:56.667
Gopal ran away
when the tragedy occurred.

473
00:30:56.792 --> 00:30:57.792
He must have gone home.

474
00:30:58.000 --> 00:30:59.542
- Go get him.
- Okay.

475
00:31:01.958 --> 00:31:03.750
Sir, a single pump won't help.

476
00:31:03.917 --> 00:31:06.875
We need at least ten pumps
to dewater continuously.

477
00:31:07.750 --> 00:31:09.000
- And Mr. Manager…
- Yes.

478
00:31:09.083 --> 00:31:12.708
Make sure there's an uninterrupted
power supply in this area. Okay?

479
00:31:12.917 --> 00:31:17.333
And inform the rail department,
to limit the speed of all trains

480
00:31:17.417 --> 00:31:20.375
on this line to less than 20.
I repeat, less than 20.

481
00:31:20.458 --> 00:31:21.750
- Got it?
<i>- Why the train?</i>

482
00:31:24.417 --> 00:31:25.875
Act faster, Mr. Manager.

483
00:31:25.958 --> 00:31:27.208
What are you doing?
Get going.

484
00:31:31.042 --> 00:31:33.625
Dayal, this incident
is very shameful for Coal India.

485
00:31:33.708 --> 00:31:35.958
- The rescue mission cannot lack effort.
- Yes, sir.

486
00:31:36.042 --> 00:31:39.542
Send the senior officers and a DGMS team
to Mahabir Colliery immediately.

487
00:31:41.833 --> 00:31:42.958
Yes, sir.

488
00:31:43.042 --> 00:31:44.625
Very sad, sir.

489
00:31:44.708 --> 00:31:48.708
Understand, Ujjwal isn't just a dedicated
CMD of ECL, but he is an old friend.

490
00:31:48.792 --> 00:31:51.042
- Yes, sir.
- Go there, take full charge.

491
00:31:51.125 --> 00:31:53.583
Use all the resources
and do the needful in the matter.

492
00:31:54.083 --> 00:31:55.417
Yes, sir. Of course, sir.

493
00:31:55.500 --> 00:31:56.500
I'm on my way, sir.

494
00:31:57.083 --> 00:31:58.483
Sir, should I bring the car around?

495
00:31:59.292 --> 00:32:00.332
You seem to be in a hurry.

496
00:32:00.583 --> 00:32:01.864
Who's going to finish this milk?

497
00:32:03.792 --> 00:32:05.625
Sir, it was me
who called Mahabir Colliery.

498
00:32:05.750 --> 00:32:08.833
Because on my way to the washroom,
I saw that the Ningha pit was open.

499
00:32:08.917 --> 00:32:09.934
And it was such a loud roar,

500
00:32:09.958 --> 00:32:11.958
like the Ganga flowing
from Lord Shiva's tresses.

501
00:32:19.042 --> 00:32:21.750
Sir, the vacuum created
by the intense water pressure

502
00:32:21.833 --> 00:32:23.292
has forced the old pit to reopen.

503
00:32:24.417 --> 00:32:26.042
Where is the entry to this incline, sir?

504
00:32:26.167 --> 00:32:27.167
That way.

505
00:32:36.833 --> 00:32:37.833
Hand me the torch.

506
00:32:41.292 --> 00:32:42.292
Be careful, Gill.

507
00:33:11.708 --> 00:33:13.875
Can we use one of these
two openings as an entry point?

508
00:33:13.958 --> 00:33:14.958
Not possible, sir.

509
00:33:15.125 --> 00:33:16.333
The water's force is too much.

510
00:33:16.583 --> 00:33:17.663
It's quite dangerous there.

511
00:33:17.833 --> 00:33:20.314
And we shouldn't send the rescue officers
through these points.

512
00:33:20.375 --> 00:33:22.083
Sir! Sir!

513
00:33:23.042 --> 00:33:24.042
Sir!

514
00:33:24.333 --> 00:33:25.333
Come quickly, sir.

515
00:33:25.625 --> 00:33:26.917
Govardhan sir has arrived.

516
00:33:27.042 --> 00:33:28.750
The matter has turned aggressive, sir.

517
00:33:31.125 --> 00:33:32.042
What did you say?

518
00:33:32.125 --> 00:33:33.833
My miners have drowned?

519
00:33:33.958 --> 00:33:35.167
Let me show you

520
00:33:35.250 --> 00:33:37.458
- what drowning to death feels like!
- Please forgive me.

521
00:33:37.542 --> 00:33:40.333
Shut up!
How dare you say such a thing?

522
00:33:40.417 --> 00:33:41.958
I'll thrash you!

523
00:33:42.042 --> 00:33:44.292
I'll throw you down the pit.

524
00:33:44.500 --> 00:33:46.083
My miners have drowned?!

525
00:33:46.167 --> 00:33:48.708
- Hit him!
- Don't spare him!

526
00:33:48.792 --> 00:33:50.833
- Hit him!
- Throw him down the pit!

527
00:33:51.958 --> 00:33:54.083
- Don't spare him.
- Sorry, sir. I didn't mean it.

528
00:33:54.167 --> 00:33:56.000
Govardhan! Govardhan!

529
00:33:56.083 --> 00:33:58.667
The union and management are
no longer friends, Ujjwal.

530
00:33:58.792 --> 00:34:00.417
I am your biggest enemy now.

531
00:34:00.500 --> 00:34:01.542
Govardhan, no!

532
00:34:02.917 --> 00:34:05.625
Our biggest enemy now is time.

533
00:34:06.042 --> 00:34:07.667
And the more we waste it,

534
00:34:07.833 --> 00:34:09.417
the harder it will get to save them.

535
00:34:09.500 --> 00:34:10.500
Govardhan, listen.

536
00:34:11.958 --> 00:34:13.375
- Everyone is stressed.
- Sir…

537
00:34:14.000 --> 00:34:15.083
I didn't mean to say that.

538
00:34:15.500 --> 00:34:16.500
Stay within your limits.

539
00:34:16.833 --> 00:34:18.074
Otherwise, I will make you pay.

540
00:34:18.375 --> 00:34:19.375
Get lost!

541
00:34:19.958 --> 00:34:21.875
Listen, Ujjwal.
This is a Bengali promising you.

542
00:34:22.750 --> 00:34:25.583
If you show any negligence
in saving my men,

543
00:34:26.042 --> 00:34:31.167
I will blow up you and your
coal company. Understood?

544
00:34:31.292 --> 00:34:32.500
And this is not an MLA,

545
00:34:32.792 --> 00:34:35.750
it's a Markatta
and a union leader speaking.

546
00:34:36.542 --> 00:34:38.500
That won't be required, brother.

547
00:34:40.083 --> 00:34:42.833
I know this area
like the back of my hand.

548
00:34:43.000 --> 00:34:44.625
- Bless me.
- Always.

549
00:34:45.958 --> 00:34:48.583
Brother, you know
I have spent eight years here.

550
00:34:48.792 --> 00:34:51.750
So headquarters called me directly

551
00:34:51.875 --> 00:34:53.833
to help the CMD.

552
00:34:53.917 --> 00:34:54.917
So, here I am.

553
00:34:55.083 --> 00:34:57.667
I have a foolproof rescue plan for you.

554
00:34:57.750 --> 00:35:00.292
I learned that the abandoned
Ningha pit has reopened.

555
00:35:00.792 --> 00:35:02.667
I'll send rescue officers down that way.

556
00:35:07.333 --> 00:35:10.542
- The Ningha abandoned pit...
- I'm sorry to interrupt you, sir.

557
00:35:10.625 --> 00:35:12.000
I just surveilled the Ningha pit...

558
00:35:13.417 --> 00:35:15.125
I am still talking, mister.

559
00:35:17.292 --> 00:35:18.292
Brother,

560
00:35:18.625 --> 00:35:20.333
I will rescue all your miners

561
00:35:21.042 --> 00:35:22.708
through Ningha pit.

562
00:35:23.125 --> 00:35:24.125
Promise.

563
00:35:24.208 --> 00:35:25.042
I expected that from you.

564
00:35:25.125 --> 00:35:28.125
This gentleman will definitely
save our families.

565
00:35:30.375 --> 00:35:32.208
Immediately call
drilling contractor Upadhyay.

566
00:35:32.292 --> 00:35:33.833
What's the point of drilling, sir?

567
00:35:33.917 --> 00:35:35.351
We'll only find dead bodies down there.

568
00:35:35.375 --> 00:35:36.695
We'll charge them for it, idiots.

569
00:35:39.458 --> 00:35:40.458
Sir!

570
00:35:40.583 --> 00:35:41.583
Sir!

571
00:35:41.833 --> 00:35:42.958
We have a problem.

572
00:35:53.083 --> 00:35:54.667
This city is full of tragedies.

573
00:35:54.750 --> 00:35:56.458
Anything can be delayed here.

574
00:35:56.542 --> 00:35:57.958
But if Rajdhani is delayed,

575
00:35:58.042 --> 00:36:00.226
I'll be facing an inquiry
from higher authorities. Understand?

576
00:36:00.250 --> 00:36:02.708
Sir, listen to me.
The water seepage in the mines

577
00:36:02.792 --> 00:36:04.083
has loosened the soil.

578
00:36:04.375 --> 00:36:08.625
If the train crosses with speed,
there is a danger surface collapsing.

579
00:36:09.125 --> 00:36:11.083
I sympathize with your situation.

580
00:36:11.375 --> 00:36:13.625
But I need permission from DRM.

581
00:36:13.708 --> 00:36:16.208
<i>And Delhi is where all
the important work is done.</i>

582
00:36:16.583 --> 00:36:18.625
<i>- Getting permission isn't easy.</i>
- Wait a minute.

583
00:36:20.500 --> 00:36:22.083
It takes months to get permission.

584
00:36:22.167 --> 00:36:23.559
He's telling me to hold for a minute.

585
00:36:23.583 --> 00:36:24.583
<i>Nonsense!</i>

586
00:36:25.292 --> 00:36:28.667
The station master is more worried
about Rajdhani being on time

587
00:36:28.958 --> 00:36:30.559
than the lives of Govardhan sir's miners.

588
00:36:30.583 --> 00:36:32.250
Go and call Govardhan sir.

589
00:36:32.333 --> 00:36:33.708
- What?
<i>- He will speak to him.</i>

590
00:36:34.083 --> 00:36:37.375
- Hello, buddy! Listen to me!
- Yes, sir.

591
00:36:37.583 --> 00:36:39.750
Don't trouble Govardhan sir.

592
00:36:39.833 --> 00:36:41.500
<i>I am talking to you, friend.</i>

593
00:36:42.667 --> 00:36:43.667
Hello? Hello?

594
00:36:43.750 --> 00:36:46.417
Sir… I'm giving the phone
to Govardhan sir.

595
00:36:46.500 --> 00:36:47.750
You explain to him.
Here you go.

596
00:36:47.833 --> 00:36:49.833
There's no need
to explain anything to him.

597
00:36:50.208 --> 00:36:51.333
I understood everything.

598
00:36:51.875 --> 00:36:53.792
You said you wanted a speed of 20, right?

599
00:36:53.875 --> 00:36:55.417
I set it to ten.

600
00:36:55.500 --> 00:36:57.083
<i>- Happy?</i>
- Happy, sir.

601
00:36:57.167 --> 00:37:00.333
Tell Govardhan sir that I got it done.

602
00:37:00.417 --> 00:37:01.417
Okay, sir.

603
00:37:02.875 --> 00:37:05.833
We were taking this
man's presence lightly.

604
00:37:06.208 --> 00:37:08.792
He's not as simple as he looks.

605
00:37:12.250 --> 00:37:13.250
Sir.

606
00:37:14.250 --> 00:37:16.708
You know entry from
Ningha pit is impossible.

607
00:37:17.958 --> 00:37:19.934
Sen is here on direct orders
from the headquarters.

608
00:37:19.958 --> 00:37:20.958
I cannot stop him.

609
00:37:21.667 --> 00:37:23.250
But we can do our job.

610
00:37:23.750 --> 00:37:24.750
How?

611
00:37:25.000 --> 00:37:26.167
I have a rescue plan.

612
00:37:26.583 --> 00:37:29.125
- Long live…
- Govardhan sir!

613
00:37:58.625 --> 00:38:02.250
Child, these gentlemen will
approve the rescue plan.

614
00:38:06.750 --> 00:38:09.833
DG sir, the mainline must
be flooded with water now.

615
00:38:10.542 --> 00:38:14.417
And if these 71 miners are still alive…

616
00:38:15.417 --> 00:38:18.583
they must be trapped near
their working area. Right?

617
00:38:18.875 --> 00:38:20.583
- Right, Sengupta?
- Right, sir.

618
00:38:20.667 --> 00:38:23.458
Ningha open pit is the nearest point
of access to them.

619
00:38:23.792 --> 00:38:24.792
From my experience,

620
00:38:24.833 --> 00:38:27.417
the water pressure
will eventually slow down.

621
00:38:27.500 --> 00:38:31.333
And my rescue officers
will climb down in the basket.

622
00:38:31.917 --> 00:38:34.083
They will find the miners and rescue them.

623
00:38:34.292 --> 00:38:35.292
Very simple.

624
00:38:35.458 --> 00:38:36.792
- Right?
- Simple, sir.

625
00:38:36.958 --> 00:38:38.750
- Then hold the chalk.
- Gill.

626
00:38:39.625 --> 00:38:42.500
Sir, among the 71 miners
trapped down there,

627
00:38:42.583 --> 00:38:45.667
many have more than
25 years of experience.

628
00:38:45.750 --> 00:38:49.500
This tells them
if the mines start flooding,

629
00:38:49.750 --> 00:38:53.667
they should head to the highest point
of the mine, and wait for rescue.

630
00:38:53.750 --> 00:38:57.750
And I believe these workers
have left their working area,

631
00:38:57.833 --> 00:38:58.833
and have made it here…

632
00:38:59.333 --> 00:39:01.500
to the highest point in the mine.

633
00:39:02.333 --> 00:39:04.792
And through a land survey,

634
00:39:04.875 --> 00:39:07.625
we can spot the highest point
of Narayankuri,

635
00:39:07.708 --> 00:39:10.667
and dig an eight-inch pilot borehole.

636
00:39:11.542 --> 00:39:16.125
And once we locate them,
we'll make another 29-inch borehole,

637
00:39:16.833 --> 00:39:19.750
send an iron capsule down,

638
00:39:19.833 --> 00:39:23.542
and rescue the miners one by one.

639
00:39:23.625 --> 00:39:25.458
Gill, has this technique

640
00:39:25.833 --> 00:39:27.833
ever been used
in a rescue mission earlier?

641
00:39:28.292 --> 00:39:29.292
No, sir.

642
00:39:29.750 --> 00:39:31.750
Rescue through capsule
will be the first in India.

643
00:39:31.833 --> 00:39:33.542
Isn't he being overly optimistic?

644
00:39:33.625 --> 00:39:35.125
I don't see any harm in that, sir.

645
00:39:35.208 --> 00:39:36.208
Gill…

646
00:39:37.417 --> 00:39:38.417
who are you?

647
00:39:38.917 --> 00:39:39.917
- Sir, I...
- Forget it.

648
00:39:40.333 --> 00:39:42.708
- Where are you from?
- I'm from SP Opencast Mines.

649
00:39:42.792 --> 00:39:44.000
Then you are not a local.

650
00:39:45.375 --> 00:39:46.875
This is not your area.

651
00:39:47.250 --> 00:39:49.333
You have no clue about
this area's condition.

652
00:39:50.083 --> 00:39:53.833
Listen, I know this area
like the back of my hand.

653
00:39:53.917 --> 00:39:54.917
He is right.

654
00:39:55.000 --> 00:39:57.125
We cannot waste time experimenting.

655
00:39:57.417 --> 00:40:00.042
Sir, we are going to lose time.

656
00:40:00.333 --> 00:40:01.374
What remains to be seen is

657
00:40:01.625 --> 00:40:04.375
whether with time,
will those families outside

658
00:40:04.792 --> 00:40:06.583
be left with a smile or grief.

659
00:40:07.542 --> 00:40:11.708
Sir, I have a question for you.
If your children were trapped in there,

660
00:40:12.208 --> 00:40:13.875
would you have tried only one option?

661
00:40:15.125 --> 00:40:17.458
I totally buy your emotional sentiments.

662
00:40:19.708 --> 00:40:23.625
But Sen's plan sounds more practical
and achievable.

663
00:40:24.792 --> 00:40:27.583
We should dedicate our resources,
energy, and manpower

664
00:40:27.917 --> 00:40:29.667
to a single rescue mission.

665
00:40:29.958 --> 00:40:33.083
Sir, Coal India has no shortage
of manpower and resources.

666
00:40:33.458 --> 00:40:35.125
I request you, sir. Please.

667
00:40:38.125 --> 00:40:40.625
Ujjwal, Gill is a junior officer.

668
00:40:41.917 --> 00:40:45.042
His failure will directly reflect
upon your leadership.

669
00:40:45.750 --> 00:40:47.292
Before taking a call,

670
00:40:47.708 --> 00:40:49.417
think it through.

671
00:41:02.708 --> 00:41:04.208
I have faith in Gill's plan.

672
00:41:06.417 --> 00:41:07.417
Fine.

673
00:41:07.708 --> 00:41:09.667
Both of you start
with your rescue plans.

674
00:41:09.750 --> 00:41:10.875
- Good luck.
- Thank you.

675
00:41:13.000 --> 00:41:14.833
Sir, I'll need two men.

676
00:41:14.917 --> 00:41:16.333
First is a drilling engineer

677
00:41:16.417 --> 00:41:18.417
- who thinks and does out of the box.
- Gill.

678
00:41:19.542 --> 00:41:20.542
Jugadu Bindal.

679
00:41:25.083 --> 00:41:26.083
Sir, call for you.

680
00:41:26.208 --> 00:41:28.292
Some Ujjwal sir is on the line.
He says it's urgent.

681
00:41:31.917 --> 00:41:33.125
Will this do, boy?

682
00:41:34.292 --> 00:41:35.542
Mother, are you happy now?

683
00:41:36.708 --> 00:41:37.708
Give me the phone!

684
00:41:39.917 --> 00:41:41.083
Yes, Ujjwal. Tell me.

685
00:41:46.792 --> 00:41:48.375
- And the other?
- Tapan Ghosh.

686
00:41:48.542 --> 00:41:50.167
- The ex-surveyor?
- Yes.

687
00:41:51.042 --> 00:41:52.042
Will he help us?

688
00:41:52.125 --> 00:41:54.417
No! I will never help you!

689
00:41:54.500 --> 00:41:55.583
Why should I help you?

690
00:41:55.792 --> 00:41:58.833
Because it's not about
the 71 miners alone, sir.

691
00:41:59.125 --> 00:42:00.500
It's about their families as well.

692
00:42:00.792 --> 00:42:02.958
What about my family?

693
00:42:03.667 --> 00:42:08.500
Coal India blamed me
for the Durgapur tragedy.

694
00:42:08.583 --> 00:42:10.542
They said the survey wasn't done right.

695
00:42:10.625 --> 00:42:12.292
The officer had no clue

696
00:42:12.375 --> 00:42:14.250
that methane gas was
forming under the rocks.

697
00:42:15.250 --> 00:42:18.708
Till today I am running
from pillar to post for my dues!

698
00:42:18.792 --> 00:42:21.458
My gratuity, my PF,
everything was stopped.

699
00:42:21.792 --> 00:42:23.059
They even threw me out of the house.

700
00:42:23.083 --> 00:42:24.500
Not to forget the court case.

701
00:42:24.583 --> 00:42:27.792
Tapan sir,
we cannot go ahead without your help.

702
00:42:27.875 --> 00:42:31.667
Because when I studied the survey map
of Mahabir Colliery with Gopal,

703
00:42:32.125 --> 00:42:33.000
this is what I noticed.

704
00:42:33.083 --> 00:42:34.625
Let me help, sir.

705
00:42:35.000 --> 00:42:36.000
Look here.

706
00:42:36.208 --> 00:42:39.083
The highest point in the mine
is shown here,

707
00:42:39.167 --> 00:42:41.458
- but the overland details are missing.
- So?

708
00:42:41.542 --> 00:42:44.833
You conducted the overland survey
of Mahabir Colliery eight years ago,

709
00:42:44.917 --> 00:42:46.997
- for mineral exploration.
- I don't remember anything.

710
00:42:47.042 --> 00:42:48.042
Leave.

711
00:42:49.708 --> 00:42:52.042
Tapan sir, you are lying.

712
00:42:52.125 --> 00:42:53.917
He is crazy. You should leave.

713
00:42:54.167 --> 00:42:57.583
- Brother.
- Sir. I was thinking we should leave.

714
00:42:57.833 --> 00:42:59.292
You are in a hurry to leave.

715
00:43:01.625 --> 00:43:02.875
Tapan sir, listen.

716
00:43:04.250 --> 00:43:08.375
Do you promise to clear my husband's dues?

717
00:43:09.583 --> 00:43:10.583
Do you promise?

718
00:43:11.125 --> 00:43:12.125
Tell me.

719
00:43:12.333 --> 00:43:13.208
Tell me.

720
00:43:13.292 --> 00:43:14.292
Answer me!

721
00:43:14.667 --> 00:43:15.667
He won't promise.

722
00:43:16.542 --> 00:43:19.833
Promises made in vulnerable situations
are often fake, sister-in-law.

723
00:43:22.958 --> 00:43:27.417
I promise I will try
my best to get you your dues.

724
00:43:28.333 --> 00:43:29.208
I will.

725
00:43:29.292 --> 00:43:30.833
Leave.

726
00:43:38.167 --> 00:43:39.167
Oh, God.

727
00:43:40.750 --> 00:43:42.292
- I need your blessings.
- Bless you.

728
00:43:52.542 --> 00:43:55.458
Let it loose. Tie it to the basket.

729
00:43:55.542 --> 00:43:56.542
Hurry up.

730
00:44:06.375 --> 00:44:09.250
- Try to understand.
- I won't go with them.

731
00:44:09.333 --> 00:44:11.042
- I'm begging you!
- No, I won't.

732
00:44:19.708 --> 00:44:22.542
You are crazy!

733
00:44:22.625 --> 00:44:23.708
Stop it!

734
00:44:26.000 --> 00:44:27.208
I am coming, Gill.

735
00:44:29.500 --> 00:44:30.833
Hurry up, guys. Keep moving.

736
00:44:32.333 --> 00:44:34.875
Stop. You can't go any further.

737
00:44:36.375 --> 00:44:39.136
Sister-in-law, it seems like Gill
has kicked off the rescue operation.

738
00:44:45.458 --> 00:44:47.833
- A little to the right.
- Put up the light poles quickly.

739
00:44:51.625 --> 00:44:54.625
- Where's Durga and Birju, Tapan sir?
- I don't know where they disappeared.

740
00:44:55.125 --> 00:44:57.125
What is the other officer's team up to?

741
00:44:57.208 --> 00:44:58.708
It's just a facade, dear.

742
00:44:58.792 --> 00:45:02.333
Tell me, what good is an eight-inch hole?

743
00:45:02.583 --> 00:45:04.583
This is a rescue operation.

744
00:45:04.833 --> 00:45:08.000
It's a matter of pride, my Bengal tigers!

745
00:45:08.083 --> 00:45:10.667
Keep it rolling.
You are doing well.

746
00:45:10.750 --> 00:45:12.792
- Lower it.
- Keep going.

747
00:45:13.167 --> 00:45:15.375
- Glory to…
- Lord Bajrangbali!

748
00:45:15.458 --> 00:45:17.583
- Glory to…
- Lord Bajrangbali!

749
00:45:17.667 --> 00:45:18.958
Prove it to the world!

750
00:45:19.042 --> 00:45:21.708
- Glory to…
- Lord Bajrangbali!

751
00:45:34.583 --> 00:45:35.583
Sengupta!

752
00:45:35.625 --> 00:45:36.542
Water!

753
00:45:36.625 --> 00:45:37.625
Water?

754
00:45:38.458 --> 00:45:39.708
What's going to happen now?

755
00:45:40.125 --> 00:45:42.083
- Goddess, please.
- Goddess, please.

756
00:45:48.708 --> 00:45:50.708
Save me!

757
00:45:51.833 --> 00:45:53.333
Hold it!

758
00:45:53.750 --> 00:45:54.870
What's happening down there?

759
00:46:00.083 --> 00:46:01.958
Oh, God!

760
00:46:02.750 --> 00:46:04.708
Save us!

761
00:46:09.083 --> 00:46:09.958
Sen sir!

762
00:46:10.042 --> 00:46:12.292
- Problem!
- Don't worry. Keep going.

763
00:46:13.500 --> 00:46:14.833
Get up!

764
00:46:19.542 --> 00:46:22.208
Sen sir, this is dangerous!

765
00:46:22.417 --> 00:46:23.333
It's okay. Keep going.

766
00:46:23.417 --> 00:46:25.083
Get us out of here!

767
00:46:25.167 --> 00:46:27.292
Sir, shall we pull them up?

768
00:46:27.375 --> 00:46:28.625
Or else they will die.

769
00:46:29.583 --> 00:46:31.208
- Pull them up.
- Okay, sir.

770
00:46:31.667 --> 00:46:32.792
Pull!

771
00:46:33.250 --> 00:46:34.917
Pull them out quickly!

772
00:46:39.917 --> 00:46:40.917
Pull!

773
00:46:44.708 --> 00:46:47.458
Pull them up. Be careful.

774
00:46:47.708 --> 00:46:51.708
- Oh, God.
- They came out.

775
00:46:52.000 --> 00:46:53.417
I don't know what's going on.

776
00:46:54.292 --> 00:46:55.292
I don't know anything.

777
00:46:56.458 --> 00:46:57.458
What will happen now?

778
00:46:59.375 --> 00:47:03.167
Sir, roughly 170 feet below this marking

779
00:47:03.417 --> 00:47:05.042
is the highest point of the mine.

780
00:47:14.958 --> 00:47:16.250
- Tapan sir.
- Yes.

781
00:47:16.333 --> 00:47:19.667
We're going to dig a 29-inch borehole
in a 100-meter radius for the capsule.

782
00:47:19.750 --> 00:47:23.208
- Pick a point.
- Gill, do you think they are still alive?

783
00:47:24.083 --> 00:47:26.208
Or waiting for us
at this point down here?

784
00:47:26.417 --> 00:47:28.333
Sir, all our efforts depend
on this hope.

785
00:47:30.625 --> 00:47:31.625
Have faith.

786
00:48:00.375 --> 00:48:02.125
Listen. Get up.

787
00:48:02.458 --> 00:48:05.125
Everyone, get up. Come on.

788
00:48:05.208 --> 00:48:08.583
Get up.
The water has reached pillar number 17.

789
00:48:09.167 --> 00:48:10.500
The water current is high.

790
00:48:10.583 --> 00:48:13.792
And it will flood this place
in the next couple of hours.

791
00:48:14.375 --> 00:48:18.000
So I suggest we head
to the highest point.

792
00:48:18.375 --> 00:48:20.917
It will take days for
that area to get flooded.

793
00:48:21.542 --> 00:48:23.500
The management will find us till then.

794
00:48:23.583 --> 00:48:25.708
It's been more than eight hours!

795
00:48:25.792 --> 00:48:27.875
Even if anyone's looking for us,

796
00:48:27.958 --> 00:48:31.208
how would they know that
we're still alive and right here?

797
00:48:31.292 --> 00:48:34.125
- Hey…
- We will all die like rodents down here.

798
00:48:34.292 --> 00:48:37.458
- Wait and watch.
- Even the CDS phone is dead!

799
00:48:37.625 --> 00:48:38.833
Damn it!

800
00:48:38.917 --> 00:48:41.042
When the surface was trying to alert us…

801
00:48:41.625 --> 00:48:45.875
if this deaf idiot had alerted us on time,

802
00:48:45.958 --> 00:48:47.750
we could have escaped.

803
00:48:47.833 --> 00:48:50.542
We are all going to drown down here!

804
00:48:50.792 --> 00:48:54.208
Rather than dying down here,
I should kill him!

805
00:48:54.417 --> 00:48:55.250
What are you doing?

806
00:48:55.333 --> 00:48:56.333
Leave him.

807
00:48:57.250 --> 00:48:59.583
I will kill you, old man!

808
00:48:59.667 --> 00:49:01.958
- Let him go.
- Let me go, Pashu!

809
00:49:02.042 --> 00:49:04.708
It's done!
What's done is done now!

810
00:49:05.750 --> 00:49:07.333
He didn't mean to do it.

811
00:49:09.042 --> 00:49:12.667
Even I am scared out of my wits.
Should I be whimpering like this?

812
00:49:13.708 --> 00:49:16.917
We know surviving is tough.

813
00:49:17.167 --> 00:49:19.333
We cannot stay here and die,
without a fight!

814
00:49:19.792 --> 00:49:20.792
Tell me.

815
00:49:22.125 --> 00:49:25.625
Your families are waiting for you.

816
00:49:26.083 --> 00:49:27.083
Right?

817
00:49:28.500 --> 00:49:29.667
Come on, Uncle.

818
00:49:29.833 --> 00:49:32.292
We have to attend
your daughter's wedding.

819
00:49:32.542 --> 00:49:36.125
The decorated bus is waiting
for us on the surface.

820
00:49:36.208 --> 00:49:38.458
Think about your daughter, Uncle.

821
00:49:43.500 --> 00:49:44.750
I have.

822
00:49:45.792 --> 00:49:49.375
If I die, my wife will get
five lakh rupees as compensation.

823
00:49:49.750 --> 00:49:51.458
Don't say stupid things!

824
00:49:51.542 --> 00:49:54.583
Right. And you are talking
like a wise man, right?

825
00:49:56.833 --> 00:50:01.500
When the night falls, Bhola,
some see darkness

826
00:50:01.625 --> 00:50:03.625
and others see stars sparkling.

827
00:50:03.708 --> 00:50:05.917
It's all in the mind.

828
00:50:06.000 --> 00:50:07.917
Pashu!

829
00:50:08.292 --> 00:50:10.292
Who knows the way up there?

830
00:50:10.375 --> 00:50:11.458
I can lead us there.

831
00:50:11.917 --> 00:50:13.292
There you go!

832
00:50:13.500 --> 00:50:15.500
Spoken like a brave heart.

833
00:50:15.792 --> 00:50:16.958
Come on. Get up.

834
00:50:17.708 --> 00:50:18.708
Get up, everyone!

835
00:50:19.208 --> 00:50:21.042
Bravo!

836
00:50:21.125 --> 00:50:24.750
Keep your hopes high.
And listen…

837
00:50:25.208 --> 00:50:27.667
Half of you will turn off your lamps.

838
00:50:27.833 --> 00:50:29.708
We must save battery.

839
00:50:29.875 --> 00:50:30.875
- Banke.
- Yes?

840
00:50:31.167 --> 00:50:33.000
- Go fetch the medical box.
- Yes, Uncle.

841
00:50:34.042 --> 00:50:35.333
Hey, Shaligram.

842
00:50:35.625 --> 00:50:36.945
You said yes with your big mouth.

843
00:50:37.125 --> 00:50:39.917
But do tell me how
you will get us up there.

844
00:50:40.000 --> 00:50:41.000
Which route?

845
00:50:41.042 --> 00:50:42.250
From pillar number 23.

846
00:50:42.708 --> 00:50:43.792
It's the only way.

847
00:50:44.125 --> 00:50:45.625
Pillar number 23.
Everyone, follow me.

848
00:50:45.708 --> 00:50:47.000
You fool!

849
00:50:47.083 --> 00:50:48.333
Look at this fool.

850
00:50:48.417 --> 00:50:51.500
Trying to be the hero himself,
and make us damsels in distress.

851
00:50:51.583 --> 00:50:54.250
Will you carry us on
your shoulders in the water?

852
00:50:54.333 --> 00:50:55.333
What water?

853
00:50:56.000 --> 00:50:58.500
- There's a stream of water in the middle...
- Shut up. Shut up.

854
00:50:58.583 --> 00:51:00.304
- Let me tell them.
- What will you tell them?

855
00:51:00.375 --> 00:51:01.375
Look here.

856
00:51:01.750 --> 00:51:03.125
This is where the water erupted.

857
00:51:04.708 --> 00:51:07.375
The water is making its way through here,

858
00:51:08.250 --> 00:51:09.875
towards Chanak.

859
00:51:11.250 --> 00:51:14.417
We are over here. Understood?

860
00:51:15.500 --> 00:51:19.583
And the high point
of the mine is over here.

861
00:51:19.792 --> 00:51:24.292
Shaligram says that we'll cross
this water and go over here.

862
00:51:25.333 --> 00:51:26.958
How will he take us across?

863
00:51:27.042 --> 00:51:28.042
Is he telling the truth?

864
00:51:28.125 --> 00:51:30.833
I told you that we took the wrong route.

865
00:51:30.917 --> 00:51:32.833
- Bloody idiots!
- I told you.

866
00:51:32.917 --> 00:51:35.125
I told you I don't
want to work in the mines.

867
00:51:35.208 --> 00:51:36.976
- Calm down, son.
- You will be responsible for my death.

868
00:51:37.000 --> 00:51:37.833
You will be okay.

869
00:51:37.917 --> 00:51:39.351
- You will be responsible for my death...
- Shut up.

870
00:51:39.375 --> 00:51:40.917
You will be responsible.

871
00:51:41.000 --> 00:51:43.042
You will be okay.

872
00:51:43.458 --> 00:51:45.875
- I am here for you.
- I don't want to die, Uncle.

873
00:51:45.958 --> 00:51:47.083
I don't want to die.

874
00:51:47.250 --> 00:51:49.083
We are still alive

875
00:51:49.167 --> 00:51:50.250
Yes!

876
00:51:50.708 --> 00:51:51.958
You are alive.

877
00:51:52.792 --> 00:51:56.708
We all saw what happened
to the miners

878
00:51:56.792 --> 00:51:58.000
when they headed to Chanak.

879
00:51:58.667 --> 00:52:01.875
The water current is too high.
Be careful. Go slow.

880
00:52:03.667 --> 00:52:04.833
Hold the wires tight.

881
00:52:06.542 --> 00:52:08.208
They barely survived.

882
00:52:09.208 --> 00:52:12.000
Until we are here, we are alive.

883
00:52:12.375 --> 00:52:14.083
If anyone goes up there,

884
00:52:14.875 --> 00:52:18.792
then you will be inviting your own death.
Remember that!

885
00:52:19.167 --> 00:52:21.792
If the management
team sends a rescue team,

886
00:52:21.917 --> 00:52:23.125
they will send them here.

887
00:52:23.208 --> 00:52:25.000
He is right!

888
00:52:25.083 --> 00:52:27.458
- We will stay right here.
- We won't go to the highest point.

889
00:52:42.625 --> 00:52:43.934
You might want to cut back
on the cigarettes.

890
00:52:43.958 --> 00:52:45.559
Your blood pressure is through the roof.

891
00:52:47.042 --> 00:52:48.042
Bindal!

892
00:52:48.417 --> 00:52:49.417
How long?

893
00:52:49.667 --> 00:52:51.307
We'll drill through in a couple of hours.

894
00:52:51.375 --> 00:52:52.250
Don't worry.

895
00:52:52.333 --> 00:52:54.250
Go unload the eight-inch pipe. Quick.

896
00:53:02.667 --> 00:53:03.667
Nirdosh.

897
00:53:04.042 --> 00:53:06.917
You have a doctor's appointment
at 5:30 p.m. tomorrow.

898
00:53:07.125 --> 00:53:09.917
If I get done here,
I'll pick you up from home.

899
00:53:10.583 --> 00:53:12.042
Otherwise, I'll send Diwakar.

900
00:53:12.125 --> 00:53:13.792
Stay where you are.

901
00:53:13.875 --> 00:53:15.542
And I don't need Diwakar either.

902
00:53:15.625 --> 00:53:18.208
<i>- I can drive on my own.</i>
- You won't drive at all.

903
00:53:18.292 --> 00:53:20.125
The doctor said you cannot drive.

904
00:53:20.208 --> 00:53:21.917
Doctors keep scaring people.

905
00:53:22.167 --> 00:53:24.625
In the village, women work
in the fields in the morning

906
00:53:24.708 --> 00:53:25.809
and deliver the baby in the evening.

907
00:53:25.833 --> 00:53:27.542
Okay, fine. Wait a minute.

908
00:53:28.458 --> 00:53:30.583
Send a message
to Goraji at the Sodapur workshop.

909
00:53:30.667 --> 00:53:32.707
Tell him to be ready
with his team tomorrow morning.

910
00:53:32.833 --> 00:53:33.833
Yes, sir.

911
00:53:34.625 --> 00:53:36.958
Nirdosh, I'll send Diwakar tomorrow.

912
00:53:37.042 --> 00:53:38.292
- Fine?
- Okay.

913
00:53:43.458 --> 00:53:45.375
We need to hurry
or we'll be in big trouble.

914
00:53:45.458 --> 00:53:46.779
Don't worry. Let me talk to them.

915
00:53:47.083 --> 00:53:48.083
Listen, guys!

916
00:53:48.500 --> 00:53:50.833
The water has reached pillar number 22.

917
00:53:50.917 --> 00:53:53.125
If we don't go now,

918
00:53:53.208 --> 00:53:55.292
gallery number 23 will get flooded.

919
00:53:55.375 --> 00:53:59.083
And we won't be able
to get to the highest point.

920
00:53:59.250 --> 00:54:01.458
This is our last chance at survival.

921
00:54:01.667 --> 00:54:02.667
Know that.

922
00:54:04.042 --> 00:54:05.125
He is right.

923
00:54:05.208 --> 00:54:06.417
Yes, he is right.

924
00:54:06.500 --> 00:54:07.417
We should go.

925
00:54:07.500 --> 00:54:08.917
Bhola, let's go.

926
00:54:19.750 --> 00:54:21.708
We did the right thing coming here.

927
00:54:22.167 --> 00:54:23.167
I'm telling you.

928
00:54:27.417 --> 00:54:29.708
I still don't trust you.

929
00:54:30.708 --> 00:54:32.375
But I am here for their sake.

930
00:54:32.792 --> 00:54:33.792
Understand?

931
00:54:36.042 --> 00:54:37.625
We'll be able to cross it. Don't worry.

932
00:54:43.875 --> 00:54:45.292
I hope everyone's tied a firm knot.

933
00:54:45.375 --> 00:54:46.917
Tie a firm knot.

934
00:54:49.417 --> 00:54:51.875
Hold each other's hands.

935
00:54:51.958 --> 00:54:53.417
- Be careful.
- Give me your hand.

936
00:54:58.000 --> 00:55:03.167
- Go, go.
- God helps those who help themselves!

937
00:55:03.750 --> 00:55:05.083
- Be careful.
- Keep moving.

938
00:55:05.708 --> 00:55:06.708
Keep moving.

939
00:55:07.417 --> 00:55:10.250
Hold on to each other. Keep moving.

940
00:55:10.708 --> 00:55:11.708
Brothers!

941
00:55:12.000 --> 00:55:13.625
The water currents are not too high.

942
00:55:13.708 --> 00:55:15.250
- Yes!
- We can get across.

943
00:55:15.333 --> 00:55:16.333
Come on.

944
00:55:18.542 --> 00:55:21.750
Glory to Goddess Tara!

945
00:55:22.208 --> 00:55:24.583
- Glory to Goddess Tara!
- Glory to Goddess Tara!

946
00:55:24.667 --> 00:55:26.625
Glory to Goddess Tara!

947
00:55:27.292 --> 00:55:28.417
- It's too high.
- Hey!

948
00:55:31.958 --> 00:55:33.167
Don't let go, Uncle!

949
00:55:33.375 --> 00:55:35.042
Glory to Goddess Tara!

950
00:55:38.667 --> 00:55:41.458
Don't let go.

951
00:55:48.167 --> 00:55:49.000
What happened?

952
00:55:49.083 --> 00:55:50.458
- What's wrong?
- Shaligram!

953
00:55:50.542 --> 00:55:52.542
- Something pierced through my foot!
- What happened?

954
00:55:52.625 --> 00:55:54.167
Everyone, watch your step!

955
00:55:56.625 --> 00:55:57.625
What happened, Shaligram?

956
00:56:01.583 --> 00:56:02.667
Be careful!

957
00:56:03.083 --> 00:56:04.208
Step back a little.

958
00:56:04.375 --> 00:56:05.625
Keep moving.

959
00:56:22.917 --> 00:56:24.717
We'll put in
the eight-inch pipe in two hours.

960
00:56:25.333 --> 00:56:26.375
I wonder what's going on.

961
00:56:26.500 --> 00:56:27.833
They won't say anything.

962
00:56:27.917 --> 00:56:29.333
They stopped working.

963
00:56:29.417 --> 00:56:31.542
- Sir, say something!
- Sir!

964
00:56:32.083 --> 00:56:34.292
They finished making
an eight-inch borehole.

965
00:56:34.375 --> 00:56:36.542
- Do you want me to celebrate?
- Tell us, sir.

966
00:56:36.625 --> 00:56:39.250
- Get lost.
- When will our family members come out?

967
00:56:39.333 --> 00:56:41.000
Why did you stop work, sir?

968
00:56:41.083 --> 00:56:42.750
Why aren't you telling us?

969
00:56:42.833 --> 00:56:45.875
- Sir!
- Did you find out anything?

970
00:56:59.333 --> 00:57:00.333
Let me see.

971
00:57:02.250 --> 00:57:04.167
Where are your mining shoes?

972
00:57:04.625 --> 00:57:06.000
- I sold them.
- Why?

973
00:57:07.417 --> 00:57:08.958
I needed the money.

974
00:57:12.000 --> 00:57:13.000
Banke.

975
00:57:13.583 --> 00:57:14.875
Fetch the medical box.

976
00:57:15.083 --> 00:57:16.083
Okay, Uncle.

977
00:57:16.125 --> 00:57:17.667
Don't use up all the antiseptic.

978
00:57:20.750 --> 00:57:22.667
What?
Others might need it.

979
00:57:25.708 --> 00:57:26.708
Pashu…

980
00:57:27.250 --> 00:57:28.875
is this what you call management?

981
00:57:29.667 --> 00:57:32.417
The medical box is all out of medicines.

982
00:57:33.833 --> 00:57:36.250
And this management
will come looking for us?

983
00:57:36.333 --> 00:57:37.333
Right?

984
00:57:37.667 --> 00:57:39.833
Curse your management!

985
00:57:39.917 --> 00:57:41.167
You are all going to die.

986
00:57:41.250 --> 00:57:42.708
No one's coming to save you.

987
00:57:43.875 --> 00:57:45.875
- We still haven't received the speaker.
- It's okay.

988
00:57:46.333 --> 00:57:47.333
Pass me the torch.

989
00:57:50.667 --> 00:57:52.167
Why are they sending a torch down?

990
00:57:58.833 --> 00:58:00.042
Glory to Lord Shiva.

991
00:58:07.500 --> 00:58:08.750
Do you think they'll find them?

992
00:58:12.542 --> 00:58:13.542
I was thinking...

993
00:58:25.500 --> 00:58:26.500
Gop!

994
00:58:26.875 --> 00:58:27.875
Daneshwar!

995
00:58:27.958 --> 00:58:28.958
Murli!

996
00:58:29.000 --> 00:58:30.250
Say something!

997
00:58:30.333 --> 00:58:33.500
If you can hear me,
come to the torch.

998
00:58:33.583 --> 00:58:35.958
- Is anybody there?
- Can they hear him?

999
00:58:36.042 --> 00:58:37.042
Shaligram!

1000
00:58:37.083 --> 00:58:38.083
Anybody there?

1001
00:58:38.917 --> 00:58:39.917
Ranjeet!

1002
00:58:40.542 --> 00:58:42.917
Can anyone hear my voice?

1003
00:58:44.292 --> 00:58:45.417
Murli?

1004
00:58:46.083 --> 00:58:47.458
Bishu?

1005
00:58:48.167 --> 00:58:49.542
Sudhama?

1006
00:58:50.292 --> 00:58:53.667
If anyone can hear me,
come to the light.

1007
00:58:55.417 --> 00:58:56.417
Keep walking.

1008
00:58:56.833 --> 00:58:58.154
We're reaching the highest point.

1009
00:58:58.750 --> 00:59:01.208
The management must be
waiting for us there.

1010
00:59:01.333 --> 00:59:02.333
Keep walking.

1011
00:59:02.833 --> 00:59:04.708
Bankelal! Gop!

1012
00:59:05.042 --> 00:59:07.042
Say something. Is anybody there?

1013
00:59:07.542 --> 00:59:08.458
Bhola?

1014
00:59:08.542 --> 00:59:09.792
Is anybody there?

1015
00:59:12.458 --> 00:59:15.125
Shaligram, I cannot walk any further.

1016
00:59:15.917 --> 00:59:17.125
How much further?

1017
00:59:17.875 --> 00:59:19.542
Just a little longer.
We're almost there.

1018
00:59:19.625 --> 00:59:21.500
Say something if you are there.

1019
00:59:22.042 --> 00:59:23.042
Pashu!

1020
00:59:23.292 --> 00:59:25.042
Can anyone hear me?

1021
00:59:27.708 --> 00:59:29.125
Say something!

1022
00:59:30.667 --> 00:59:32.583
How much further?

1023
00:59:32.667 --> 00:59:33.667
Pashu.

1024
00:59:33.792 --> 00:59:34.792
Yeah?

1025
00:59:35.958 --> 00:59:36.958
Did you see that?

1026
00:59:48.542 --> 00:59:49.542
Let's go.

1027
01:00:15.917 --> 01:00:17.000
What happened, Gill?

1028
01:00:18.333 --> 01:00:19.458
No one's responding.

1029
01:00:19.542 --> 01:00:20.708
It's game over, I guess.

1030
01:00:21.750 --> 01:00:22.750
What happened?

1031
01:00:36.000 --> 01:00:37.000
Noor!

1032
01:00:37.167 --> 01:00:38.167
Murli!

1033
01:00:38.375 --> 01:00:40.375
Can anyone hear my voice?

1034
01:00:40.917 --> 01:00:42.167
Say something.

1035
01:00:42.500 --> 01:00:43.333
Anybody there?

1036
01:00:43.417 --> 01:00:47.500
If anyone can hear me,
come to the light.

1037
01:00:47.792 --> 01:00:48.875
Is anybody there?

1038
01:00:52.000 --> 01:00:53.000
We are here, guys.

1039
01:00:53.542 --> 01:00:57.375
Pashu, you said the management
will be waiting for us here.

1040
01:00:57.458 --> 01:00:58.708
Calm down.

1041
01:00:58.958 --> 01:01:00.833
This is the highest point of the mine.

1042
01:01:01.375 --> 01:01:03.250
We will wait out here.

1043
01:01:03.333 --> 01:01:04.542
- Right.
- Brothers.

1044
01:01:05.000 --> 01:01:07.208
The management will find us soon.

1045
01:01:07.625 --> 01:01:09.792
- Everyone be seated until then.
- Sit down.

1046
01:01:10.167 --> 01:01:11.583
Let's get some rest till then.

1047
01:01:12.125 --> 01:01:13.542
- Come on.
- Sit.

1048
01:01:13.625 --> 01:01:14.625
Get some rest.

1049
01:01:15.125 --> 01:01:16.125
Gop!

1050
01:01:17.917 --> 01:01:19.042
Daneshwar!

1051
01:01:20.958 --> 01:01:22.083
Say something.

1052
01:01:22.458 --> 01:01:23.458
Bansi!

1053
01:01:23.792 --> 01:01:24.792
Narayan!

1054
01:01:31.333 --> 01:01:32.333
Ranjeet!

1055
01:01:33.083 --> 01:01:34.208
Shaligram!

1056
01:01:35.667 --> 01:01:37.417
Come to the light!

1057
01:01:42.750 --> 01:01:43.875
Is anybody there?

1058
01:01:46.333 --> 01:01:48.333
Say something.
Is anybody there?

1059
01:01:58.000 --> 01:01:59.000
Hello.

1060
01:01:59.375 --> 01:02:00.292
Why won't you tell us anything?

1061
01:02:00.375 --> 01:02:02.375
- Call your seniors.
- Call him!

1062
01:02:02.625 --> 01:02:03.625
Yes, sir.

1063
01:02:03.958 --> 01:02:06.208
A negative result
from both the teams, sir.

1064
01:02:07.000 --> 01:02:09.250
And unfortunately, now there is no hope.

1065
01:02:10.167 --> 01:02:11.583
Yes, sir.
Okay.

1066
01:02:14.000 --> 01:02:16.875
Considering the present situation,
the chairman has decided

1067
01:02:17.375 --> 01:02:18.708
to stop the rescue operation.

1068
01:02:19.500 --> 01:02:20.500
Quite tragic.

1069
01:02:21.375 --> 01:02:23.542
Tragic! But the fact is…

1070
01:02:24.458 --> 01:02:25.917
if the miners were alive,

1071
01:02:26.917 --> 01:02:29.750
nothing could have stopped them
from getting to the highest point.

1072
01:02:33.958 --> 01:02:34.958
Gill sir.

1073
01:02:35.083 --> 01:02:36.458
Sir, come with me.

1074
01:02:36.792 --> 01:02:37.792
Please.

1075
01:02:43.083 --> 01:02:44.958
Which new conference has begun now?

1076
01:02:47.958 --> 01:02:48.958
I am sure about it.

1077
01:02:52.167 --> 01:02:53.458
You're right, Mr. Sen.

1078
01:02:53.958 --> 01:02:57.292
If miners are alive, nothing can stop
them from reaching the highest point.

1079
01:02:57.375 --> 01:02:59.708
- Yes.
- But a stoppage wall can.

1080
01:03:00.500 --> 01:03:04.250
Twelve years ago, I surveyed this mine
and identified two locations

1081
01:03:04.333 --> 01:03:05.542
for the stoppage walls.

1082
01:03:05.625 --> 01:03:06.625
One over here.

1083
01:03:07.083 --> 01:03:08.843
And another over here,
at this highest point.

1084
01:03:09.042 --> 01:03:11.250
We have details of this wall.

1085
01:03:11.417 --> 01:03:13.750
But this wall's details are missing.

1086
01:03:14.042 --> 01:03:17.042
Sir, there are bright chances
that there is a wall in this area.

1087
01:03:17.292 --> 01:03:20.417
And they will be waiting for us
on the other side of the wall.

1088
01:03:20.917 --> 01:03:23.625
Sir, I want permission
to dig one more borehole.

1089
01:03:23.708 --> 01:03:27.333
Gill, don't waste
Coal India's money like this.

1090
01:03:27.625 --> 01:03:31.083
- It's an old method to make money.
- Just a minute, Sen.

1091
01:03:31.458 --> 01:03:33.917
Gill, if there's any stoppage wall.

1092
01:03:34.125 --> 01:03:36.125
Why didn't they break it and come forward?

1093
01:03:36.208 --> 01:03:38.042
Because there's an inclination.

1094
01:03:38.250 --> 01:03:41.167
And that's why water moved towards Chanak.

1095
01:03:41.333 --> 01:03:43.667
But there are so many galleries.

1096
01:03:43.875 --> 01:03:45.315
Why hasn't water flown to that side?

1097
01:03:45.500 --> 01:03:50.167
Son, what will you gain
by adding up your knowledge?

1098
01:03:51.042 --> 01:03:55.083
It would be best
if all of us started praying now.

1099
01:03:55.167 --> 01:03:56.250
Listen to me, Banke.

1100
01:03:56.500 --> 01:03:58.500
After extracting the coal,

1101
01:03:58.625 --> 01:04:01.875
a stoppage wall of bricks
is erected in the gallery.

1102
01:04:02.250 --> 01:04:04.875
To avoid loss of oxygen.

1103
01:04:05.417 --> 01:04:06.417
That's why.

1104
01:04:06.875 --> 01:04:07.875
Understood?

1105
01:04:33.000 --> 01:04:34.000
A wall of bricks?

1106
01:04:36.333 --> 01:04:37.875
This isn't the highest point!

1107
01:04:38.375 --> 01:04:40.542
Pashu, this is the stoppage wall.

1108
01:04:40.875 --> 01:04:42.083
It's a brick wall.

1109
01:04:42.167 --> 01:04:43.875
We are waiting
at the wrong spot, brothers!

1110
01:04:43.958 --> 01:04:44.958
What are you saying?

1111
01:04:45.167 --> 01:04:46.167
Mr. Sen.

1112
01:04:51.500 --> 01:04:52.500
Really?

1113
01:04:52.708 --> 01:04:54.917
- Go, get some warm milk. Go.
- Okay.

1114
01:04:55.375 --> 01:04:57.708
Sir, my PA says that
six deceased miners' bodies

1115
01:04:57.792 --> 01:05:00.417
have been discovered
in Mahavir Colliery's pit number one.

1116
01:05:00.875 --> 01:05:01.875
What?!

1117
01:05:05.000 --> 01:05:06.375
Oh, God!

1118
01:05:07.250 --> 01:05:08.250
Now, tell me, sir.

1119
01:05:08.500 --> 01:05:10.167
Do you still hope that they are alive?

1120
01:05:10.917 --> 01:05:13.208
Ujjwal, we tried our best.

1121
01:05:13.500 --> 01:05:14.750
But it was their destiny.

1122
01:05:15.125 --> 01:05:16.125
Correct.

1123
01:05:16.500 --> 01:05:20.375
Ujjwal sir, be thankful to God
that there were only 71 people…

1124
01:05:21.875 --> 01:05:24.208
and not more than 200 people,
like in Chasnala.

1125
01:05:24.792 --> 01:05:25.792
Right?

1126
01:05:26.792 --> 01:05:31.750
Sir, I think we should grant permission
for one more borehole.

1127
01:05:32.792 --> 01:05:33.958
What are you saying, Ujjwal?

1128
01:05:34.583 --> 01:05:35.667
The decision has been made.

1129
01:05:36.167 --> 01:05:37.807
You please make an official announcement.

1130
01:05:46.500 --> 01:05:47.809
Lift it carefully. Lift it overhead.

1131
01:05:47.833 --> 01:05:50.167
Keep moving it carefully.

1132
01:05:52.292 --> 01:05:53.292
CMD sir is here.

1133
01:05:54.375 --> 01:05:55.458
Lift it overhead.

1134
01:05:56.458 --> 01:05:58.000
Careful, everyone!

1135
01:06:02.875 --> 01:06:03.875
Go away.

1136
01:06:04.083 --> 01:06:05.458
The rescue operation is over.

1137
01:06:06.292 --> 01:06:08.500
Say something, sir.
What's going on?

1138
01:06:08.583 --> 01:06:10.458
CMD sir, tell us something.

1139
01:06:10.917 --> 01:06:11.792
Please tell us.

1140
01:06:11.875 --> 01:06:14.500
- Lift it. Hurry up.
- Charge!

1141
01:06:16.333 --> 01:06:17.333
Harder!

1142
01:06:17.958 --> 01:06:19.375
Harder!

1143
01:06:20.000 --> 01:06:21.625
We did it!

1144
01:06:22.042 --> 01:06:23.167
What do you see, Pashu?

1145
01:06:24.792 --> 01:06:25.792
Tell us!

1146
01:06:26.333 --> 01:06:28.500
Management is searching for us.

1147
01:06:28.583 --> 01:06:29.792
They've sent a torch.

1148
01:06:29.875 --> 01:06:32.667
- Glory to Goddess Kali!
- Glory to Goddess Kali!

1149
01:06:33.667 --> 01:06:36.000
- Sir, please tell us.
- Did you find anything?

1150
01:06:36.083 --> 01:06:37.458
Why are they quiet?

1151
01:06:37.542 --> 01:06:38.958
Please say something, sir.

1152
01:06:39.167 --> 01:06:41.333
You said you would help them.

1153
01:06:42.458 --> 01:06:44.458
- Sir, please, tell us.
- Say something.

1154
01:06:44.583 --> 01:06:45.917
I can't do this.

1155
01:06:49.000 --> 01:06:50.500
Where are you going?

1156
01:06:50.583 --> 01:06:51.917
Sir, what's going on?

1157
01:06:52.833 --> 01:06:54.750
Please tell us something, sir.

1158
01:06:56.750 --> 01:06:59.542
Sir, please say something.

1159
01:07:00.792 --> 01:07:02.333
Say something!

1160
01:07:02.417 --> 01:07:03.417
Say something.

1161
01:07:03.500 --> 01:07:06.500
Sorry, we couldn't find…

1162
01:07:08.292 --> 01:07:11.167
- your family members.
- What are you saying, sir?!

1163
01:07:11.750 --> 01:07:13.083
Don't say that, sir!

1164
01:07:13.917 --> 01:07:15.333
On the company's orders,

1165
01:07:16.208 --> 01:07:20.250
we have stopped the rescue operation.

1166
01:07:20.333 --> 01:07:22.500
- How can you do this?
- You cannot do this, sir.

1167
01:07:26.292 --> 01:07:27.542
Please forgive me.

1168
01:07:29.125 --> 01:07:30.125
Come on, brothers.

1169
01:07:30.250 --> 01:07:32.333
Let's go. Hurry up.

1170
01:07:32.583 --> 01:07:33.750
Hurry up, everyone.

1171
01:07:34.292 --> 01:07:36.417
Was all this just a charade?

1172
01:08:08.500 --> 01:08:09.958
Don't pull the torch!

1173
01:08:10.042 --> 01:08:11.750
Don't pull the torch, please!

1174
01:08:12.167 --> 01:08:14.292
Hey, we are alive!

1175
01:08:14.875 --> 01:08:19.000
- Stop!
- We are alive down here!

1176
01:08:19.083 --> 01:08:20.667
Stop!

1177
01:08:22.458 --> 01:08:24.625
We are alive!

1178
01:08:26.750 --> 01:08:27.750
Stop!

1179
01:08:28.125 --> 01:08:29.792
Is anyone there?

1180
01:08:30.125 --> 01:08:31.583
We are alive!

1181
01:08:31.667 --> 01:08:33.125
We are here!

1182
01:08:33.208 --> 01:08:35.833
- Is anybody listening?
- We are alive!

1183
01:08:35.917 --> 01:08:38.458
- Is anybody there?
- We are alive!

1184
01:08:38.542 --> 01:08:39.750
We are here!

1185
01:08:45.083 --> 01:08:46.958
Calm down, everyone!

1186
01:08:48.375 --> 01:08:51.125
God will not forgive you for this, sir!

1187
01:08:53.792 --> 01:08:55.250
We have to face this.

1188
01:08:58.667 --> 01:09:00.042
We are alive!

1189
01:09:00.708 --> 01:09:01.792
I can hear something.

1190
01:09:23.250 --> 01:09:25.125
Hey, is anyone listening?

1191
01:09:25.208 --> 01:09:27.042
We are alive!

1192
01:09:29.458 --> 01:09:31.000
Is anyone out there?

1193
01:09:32.333 --> 01:09:33.375
Ujjwal sir!

1194
01:09:35.083 --> 01:09:36.458
Sir, they are alive!

1195
01:09:36.875 --> 01:09:38.000
We found them!

1196
01:09:38.750 --> 01:09:40.042
They are alive!

1197
01:09:42.375 --> 01:09:43.583
They are alive!

1198
01:09:44.333 --> 01:09:48.000
- We found them! They are alive!
- My husband is alive!

1199
01:09:48.250 --> 01:09:49.333
They are alive.

1200
01:09:50.917 --> 01:09:52.500
They are alive!

1201
01:09:59.208 --> 01:10:03.167
We've found you!
Can you hear us?

1202
01:10:03.917 --> 01:10:05.958
We've found you.

1203
01:10:06.042 --> 01:10:08.458
They have found us!

1204
01:10:08.542 --> 01:10:10.042
We'll soon go back to our families.

1205
01:10:10.125 --> 01:10:11.625
Glory to Goddess Tara!

1206
01:10:15.917 --> 01:10:17.875
<i>It's all Your doing, God.</i>

1207
01:10:20.125 --> 01:10:22.792
Sen, why am I getting this bad news now?

1208
01:10:23.125 --> 01:10:24.434
And who is this Jaswant Singh Gill?

1209
01:10:24.458 --> 01:10:25.958
He's nobody, sir.

1210
01:10:26.042 --> 01:10:28.750
And this "nobody" has found
the rest of the 65 miners,

1211
01:10:28.833 --> 01:10:29.914
is that what you're saying?

1212
01:10:30.125 --> 01:10:33.667
Finding the miners is only
ten percent of the rescue operation.

1213
01:10:34.042 --> 01:10:35.917
<i>Gill's problem will start now.</i>

1214
01:10:36.000 --> 01:10:39.375
Because getting them
out alive and safely

1215
01:10:39.458 --> 01:10:41.167
is the real rescue operation, sir.

1216
01:10:42.000 --> 01:10:45.000
Gill's 29-inch borehole
will not work, sir.

1217
01:10:45.083 --> 01:10:46.000
Better for you, Sen.

1218
01:10:46.083 --> 01:10:47.417
<i>- And remember, Sen.</i>
- Yes?

1219
01:10:47.500 --> 01:10:49.375
I had sent you to ruin Ujjwal's career.

1220
01:10:49.583 --> 01:10:51.917
Make sure the plan doesn't backfire on me!

1221
01:10:54.917 --> 01:10:56.208
Send the medicines down.

1222
01:10:56.583 --> 01:10:57.943
We're sending medicines for Behra.

1223
01:10:58.208 --> 01:11:00.417
Sir, is it important to do this?

1224
01:11:01.000 --> 01:11:02.184
What if the miners get nervous?

1225
01:11:02.208 --> 01:11:03.208
This is the right time.

1226
01:11:03.958 --> 01:11:05.833
They will be focused on eating now.

1227
01:11:08.333 --> 01:11:09.917
Why are they taking the lantern?

1228
01:11:10.000 --> 01:11:12.667
This isn't a lantern,
it is Davy's lamp.

1229
01:11:12.750 --> 01:11:16.417
It's used to check the formation
of poisonous gas in the mine.

1230
01:11:22.375 --> 01:11:24.083
Pashu, listen to me carefully.

1231
01:11:24.250 --> 01:11:25.250
Yes, sir.

1232
01:11:35.708 --> 01:11:36.708
Lamp?

1233
01:11:37.208 --> 01:11:38.375
Why have they sent this lamp?

1234
01:11:39.750 --> 01:11:41.583
Is any gas forming here?

1235
01:11:41.667 --> 01:11:43.625
- What did you say? Gas?
- Gas?

1236
01:11:43.958 --> 01:11:45.917
Why are you scaring everyone?

1237
01:11:46.000 --> 01:11:48.667
It's a precautionary measure.
Don't you all know?

1238
01:11:48.750 --> 01:11:50.333
- Right?
- Don't worry.

1239
01:11:50.417 --> 01:11:51.542
- Take this.
- Give it here.

1240
01:11:52.167 --> 01:11:53.167
Let me check.

1241
01:12:20.667 --> 01:12:22.125
Your clothes shouldn't be wet.

1242
01:12:22.208 --> 01:12:23.329
Remove them before entering.

1243
01:13:15.458 --> 01:13:19.375
Start numbering the pillar
from where the gas is detected.

1244
01:13:24.625 --> 01:13:26.000
ONE

1245
01:13:30.208 --> 01:13:31.208
FIVE

1246
01:13:33.708 --> 01:13:34.708
ELEVEN

1247
01:13:36.958 --> 01:13:38.625
FIFTEEN

1248
01:13:53.875 --> 01:13:54.875
NINETEEN

1249
01:13:59.167 --> 01:14:00.292
TWENTY

1250
01:14:00.625 --> 01:14:02.250
There's no danger here.

1251
01:14:02.708 --> 01:14:05.375
There's no sign of water or gas.

1252
01:14:05.542 --> 01:14:06.862
How many pillars away is the gas?

1253
01:14:06.917 --> 01:14:09.208
No, sir. Don't you worry about that.

1254
01:14:09.708 --> 01:14:12.333
We have entered the mine nearly 20 times.

1255
01:14:12.583 --> 01:14:13.583
Right, brothers?

1256
01:14:13.625 --> 01:14:14.750
Which gas is forming?

1257
01:14:16.042 --> 01:14:17.417
- Methane?
- No, sir.

1258
01:14:18.375 --> 01:14:19.500
Fruits are plenty here.

1259
01:14:20.333 --> 01:14:22.917
- Carbon dioxide?
- Correct, sir.

1260
01:14:23.208 --> 01:14:26.375
Send some snacks and sweets, too.

1261
01:14:29.000 --> 01:14:30.208
Sir, miners are here.

1262
01:14:30.417 --> 01:14:31.958
And the rescue borehole spot is here.

1263
01:14:32.542 --> 01:14:34.875
DG sir, according to Pashu…

1264
01:14:35.000 --> 01:14:37.875
carbon dioxide gas and water
are 20 pillars away,

1265
01:14:37.958 --> 01:14:40.875
which is only 3000 feet away
from the miners.

1266
01:14:41.417 --> 01:14:43.833
Both of these are not in our control.

1267
01:14:43.917 --> 01:14:46.542
And with the rate at which
the water level and gas are rising,

1268
01:14:46.708 --> 01:14:50.875
we only have 48 hours
to save these miners.

1269
01:14:50.958 --> 01:14:51.792
What?

1270
01:14:51.917 --> 01:14:53.125
Then start immediately, Gill.

1271
01:14:53.792 --> 01:14:57.125
Sir, how much time will it take
to make a borehole of 29 inches?

1272
01:14:57.208 --> 01:15:01.167
We need to dig it in three stages.
8-inch, 12-inch, and then 29-inch.

1273
01:15:01.250 --> 01:15:03.375
It will take approximately 40 hours.

1274
01:15:03.458 --> 01:15:04.708
That will be cut to cut.

1275
01:15:04.792 --> 01:15:06.226
- How will it be possible?
- What do you mean?

1276
01:15:06.250 --> 01:15:09.542
There's no drill bit bigger
than eight inches in the whole of Bengal?

1277
01:15:09.625 --> 01:15:14.000
How will Bindal make
12-inch and 29-inch boreholes?

1278
01:15:14.833 --> 01:15:15.833
Don't you worry!

1279
01:15:16.083 --> 01:15:17.083
I will do it quickly.

1280
01:15:17.500 --> 01:15:18.500
Tapeshwar.

1281
01:15:22.458 --> 01:15:24.333
Do you doubt me, sir?

1282
01:15:24.708 --> 01:15:26.833
Our association is so old, sir.

1283
01:15:26.917 --> 01:15:27.917
Have you forgotten?

1284
01:15:28.333 --> 01:15:32.000
Gill's idea of rescuing miners
through the capsule is not safe.

1285
01:15:33.000 --> 01:15:34.917
I see. What's your idea then?

1286
01:15:35.292 --> 01:15:37.208
Very simple, DG sir. See this.

1287
01:15:38.125 --> 01:15:40.125
Gill is attempting rescue from this point.

1288
01:15:40.208 --> 01:15:41.667
- Correct.
- And…

1289
01:15:41.750 --> 01:15:44.750
we will reach the miners
by cutting the incline from here.

1290
01:15:45.417 --> 01:15:47.309
Only one miner can come up
from the capsule at a time.

1291
01:15:47.333 --> 01:15:51.250
On the contrary, miners will walk
on this incline and come out all at once.

1292
01:15:51.542 --> 01:15:53.875
It will take some time.
But it's safe, sir.

1293
01:15:53.958 --> 01:15:54.958
I agree.

1294
01:15:56.500 --> 01:15:58.125
Let Gill continue with his idea.

1295
01:15:58.583 --> 01:15:59.750
You too start your work.

1296
01:15:59.958 --> 01:16:01.375
- Okay?
- Yes.

1297
01:16:03.917 --> 01:16:04.917
Okay?

1298
01:16:05.875 --> 01:16:07.000
Govardhan sir, tea.

1299
01:16:07.375 --> 01:16:08.625
Is my father alright, sir?

1300
01:16:08.750 --> 01:16:10.083
Please tell me, sir.

1301
01:16:10.167 --> 01:16:11.750
If I could talk to him…

1302
01:16:11.958 --> 01:16:13.278
Everyone can talk to their family

1303
01:16:13.458 --> 01:16:15.208
after the doctor sends
medicines downstairs.

1304
01:16:15.625 --> 01:16:19.375
I want all of you to go home and rest.

1305
01:16:19.458 --> 01:16:21.667
- We are here, right?
- We all will stay right here.

1306
01:16:21.750 --> 01:16:23.708
- With you.
- Yes, sir.

1307
01:16:23.792 --> 01:16:26.375
Please, forgive me, sir.

1308
01:16:27.042 --> 01:16:29.833
I made a huge mistake in anger.

1309
01:16:29.917 --> 01:16:32.125
I slapped you.

1310
01:16:32.208 --> 01:16:34.249
- No. No. Please, don't say that.
- Please forgive me.

1311
01:16:34.500 --> 01:16:37.583
I would have reacted just like you
had I been in your position.

1312
01:16:38.292 --> 01:16:39.917
I am sorry, sir.

1313
01:16:45.083 --> 01:16:49.042
<i>When we tread together we shall win</i>

1314
01:16:49.917 --> 01:16:54.250
<i>When we walk hand in hand we shall win</i>

1315
01:16:57.667 --> 01:17:02.458
<i>Keep every promise we made
Every claim we made</i>

1316
01:17:02.917 --> 01:17:07.750
<i>Our determination will win</i>

1317
01:17:08.042 --> 01:17:13.125
<i>We will overcome every difficulty
Every hurdle</i>

1318
01:17:13.417 --> 01:17:18.292
<i>We will win every heart
Every mind</i>

1319
01:17:18.375 --> 01:17:22.042
<i>When we tread together, we shall win</i>

1320
01:17:22.958 --> 01:17:29.083
<i>When we walk hand in hand, we shall win</i>

1321
01:17:29.167 --> 01:17:33.000
<i>We know will win</i>

1322
01:17:34.417 --> 01:17:38.792
<i>Promise that we will win</i>

1323
01:17:39.417 --> 01:17:43.792
<i>We will overcome every difficulty
Every hurdle</i>

1324
01:17:45.083 --> 01:17:49.208
<i>Unite with our kin again</i>

1325
01:17:50.125 --> 01:17:54.458
<i>We will overcome every difficulty
Every hurdle</i>

1326
01:17:55.750 --> 01:18:01.083
<i>Unite with our kin again</i>

1327
01:18:04.500 --> 01:18:08.958
Mahabir mine accident led to landslides
like this at many places.

1328
01:18:13.792 --> 01:18:15.417
My home, sir!

1329
01:18:15.500 --> 01:18:18.143
We're left with no choice. That's why
we are demolishing your houses.

1330
01:18:18.167 --> 01:18:19.375
I think about everyone.

1331
01:18:22.958 --> 01:18:27.750
<i>If we can be one heart and soul</i>

1332
01:18:28.250 --> 01:18:30.750
<i>Then we shall overcome…</i>

1333
01:18:30.875 --> 01:18:31.875
He's asleep.

1334
01:18:33.333 --> 01:18:38.542
<i>Otherwise, this victory</i>

1335
01:18:38.917 --> 01:18:43.375
<i>Will not be worth celebrating</i>

1336
01:18:43.458 --> 01:18:45.500
<i>Don't let go of my hand</i>

1337
01:18:46.167 --> 01:18:48.292
<i>Don't lose your determination</i>

1338
01:18:48.792 --> 01:18:51.208
<i>Together if we face the storms</i>

1339
01:18:51.417 --> 01:18:54.625
<i>Then we shall overcome</i>

1340
01:18:57.542 --> 01:19:01.708
Sir, what if this 12-inch
locally made plate is broken?

1341
01:19:01.792 --> 01:19:04.292
Then Gill's rescue operation
will be a total flop.

1342
01:19:04.708 --> 01:19:05.989
Are you a pessimist since birth?

1343
01:19:06.542 --> 01:19:08.167
Or is this a freshly infested disease?

1344
01:19:08.292 --> 01:19:09.458
Be swift, man.

1345
01:19:11.083 --> 01:19:13.208
Sir, the gas has reached
pillar number six.

1346
01:19:30.042 --> 01:19:31.958
Glory to Lord Bajrangbali!

1347
01:19:32.083 --> 01:19:33.083
Turn it on.

1348
01:19:40.250 --> 01:19:41.542
Lord Almighty…

1349
01:19:52.625 --> 01:19:57.083
Hey, it worked!
The idea is successful!

1350
01:19:58.542 --> 01:20:01.458
Glory to Lord Bajrangbali!

1351
01:20:02.292 --> 01:20:04.667
Glory to Lord Bajrangbali!

1352
01:20:04.750 --> 01:20:06.710
The way this blade
is cutting through the surface,

1353
01:20:06.917 --> 01:20:09.417
it will cut through 150 feet like butter.

1354
01:20:09.917 --> 01:20:11.042
Good job, Bindal.

1355
01:20:18.625 --> 01:20:19.666
What's the matter, Bindal?

1356
01:20:20.000 --> 01:20:21.000
I made a mistake.

1357
01:20:21.667 --> 01:20:22.667
What do you mean?

1358
01:20:23.375 --> 01:20:25.917
My crane will not work here.

1359
01:20:26.000 --> 01:20:27.792
This crane's height is 110 feet tall.

1360
01:20:27.875 --> 01:20:29.667
To move the capsule up and down,

1361
01:20:29.750 --> 01:20:33.333
we need a 150-foot tall,
12-ton marshal crane.

1362
01:20:36.750 --> 01:20:37.910
- You will get it.
- From where?

1363
01:20:39.042 --> 01:20:40.083
It's on Sen's site.

1364
01:20:40.625 --> 01:20:41.792
Then the problem is solved.

1365
01:20:42.000 --> 01:20:43.083
God is great!

1366
01:20:46.583 --> 01:20:48.250
Sir, things there are not fine.

1367
01:20:49.167 --> 01:20:51.833
We will reach the miners
quickly through this incline.

1368
01:20:54.708 --> 01:20:57.833
At present, the incline work has stopped.

1369
01:20:58.917 --> 01:21:01.083
Sir, I've decided…

1370
01:21:01.375 --> 01:21:04.083
- to blast that rock.
- Stop boasting.

1371
01:21:04.333 --> 01:21:05.333
The passage will be…

1372
01:21:05.375 --> 01:21:07.375
The entire village will sink,
do you have any idea?

1373
01:21:07.667 --> 01:21:10.208
This ambition you have to replace Ujjwal

1374
01:21:10.667 --> 01:21:14.000
and become the CMD of this area
will not be fulfilled with such a mindset.

1375
01:21:14.583 --> 01:21:15.583
Don't mind, sir.

1376
01:21:16.167 --> 01:21:17.833
It was my turn to be promoted.

1377
01:21:19.208 --> 01:21:21.583
But Ujjwal was made CMD instead.

1378
01:21:21.792 --> 01:21:23.208
And only because…

1379
01:21:23.875 --> 01:21:26.075
he has experience working
in the coal fields of England.

1380
01:21:26.292 --> 01:21:29.083
And the selection committee forgot
I was born in England as well.

1381
01:21:29.167 --> 01:21:31.500
Even I have a British passport.
Same as Ujjwal.

1382
01:21:31.917 --> 01:21:35.375
All I mean to say is
that the public should feel…

1383
01:21:35.708 --> 01:21:37.458
we are sincerely trying to save them.

1384
01:21:38.042 --> 01:21:40.417
Actually, the result is zero.

1385
01:21:46.125 --> 01:21:48.167
Terrible tragedy, Ujjwal.

1386
01:21:48.458 --> 01:21:49.458
You must be Gill.

1387
01:21:49.792 --> 01:21:51.583
I've heard a lot of
good things about you.

1388
01:21:52.292 --> 01:21:54.583
Are you sure your rescue plan will work?

1389
01:21:54.667 --> 01:21:55.750
- Yes, sir.
- No, sir.

1390
01:21:56.208 --> 01:21:58.667
The land has already softened.
The village will sink.

1391
01:21:58.875 --> 01:22:00.417
Look. It's already sinking.

1392
01:22:01.583 --> 01:22:02.583
Sen is right, Ujjwal.

1393
01:22:02.667 --> 01:22:06.958
Mr. Gill,
I've spent eight years in this area.

1394
01:22:07.125 --> 01:22:09.708
- I know this area like...
- I've spent 24 hours here,

1395
01:22:09.792 --> 01:22:12.583
and now I know this area
like the back of my hand.

1396
01:22:13.625 --> 01:22:16.625
The land is soft only until 25 feet.

1397
01:22:16.750 --> 01:22:19.083
We will install these
casing up to 25 feet.

1398
01:22:19.708 --> 01:22:22.469
It will prevent the ground from sinking
for about eight to nine hours.

1399
01:22:22.792 --> 01:22:25.500
During that time,
we'll get the miners out comfortably.

1400
01:22:25.583 --> 01:22:28.083
- There's no use in having this discussion.
- Sen.

1401
01:22:29.333 --> 01:22:30.708
Discussion is a must.

1402
01:22:31.333 --> 01:22:32.667
It guarantees good results.

1403
01:22:33.750 --> 01:22:37.208
Sen, we will need
your 150-foot tall crane.

1404
01:22:37.292 --> 01:22:39.875
Come on, Ujjwal!
You need not ask.

1405
01:22:40.458 --> 01:22:42.167
- Sen.
- Consider it done, sir.

1406
01:22:42.292 --> 01:22:44.750
Ujjwal, after all, we are batting
for the same team.

1407
01:22:45.500 --> 01:22:46.958
You are smart.

1408
01:22:47.875 --> 01:22:48.875
Gill…

1409
01:22:50.000 --> 01:22:51.375
keep up the good work.

1410
01:22:52.792 --> 01:22:53.792
Thank you, sir.

1411
01:22:54.208 --> 01:22:55.833
- Let's go, Sen.
- Yes, sir.

1412
01:23:02.125 --> 01:23:03.917
Sir, something is going on
in their minds.

1413
01:23:04.000 --> 01:23:05.667
Do you remember that German tender?

1414
01:23:05.792 --> 01:23:07.708
The 108-crore coal handling plant?

1415
01:23:07.792 --> 01:23:09.167
It was only worth 80 crores.

1416
01:23:09.667 --> 01:23:12.125
I stopped them from scamming 28 crores.

1417
01:23:12.292 --> 01:23:14.750
Now that they have a chance,
they are trying to pull me down.

1418
01:23:17.958 --> 01:23:18.958
Don't worry, sir.

1419
01:23:19.958 --> 01:23:21.625
This time also they won't succeed.

1420
01:23:22.208 --> 01:23:23.208
Sir, please.

1421
01:23:25.958 --> 01:23:27.292
You called him a "nobody", right?

1422
01:23:27.667 --> 01:23:30.625
- Sir, I...
- Sen, if his plan fails,

1423
01:23:30.833 --> 01:23:32.000
we will definitely benefit.

1424
01:23:32.250 --> 01:23:35.208
But if his plan is successful,

1425
01:23:36.167 --> 01:23:38.500
then make sure we get the credit.

1426
01:23:38.792 --> 01:23:39.875
Yes, sir.

1427
01:23:40.833 --> 01:23:41.833
Careful. Be careful.

1428
01:23:41.875 --> 01:23:45.542
You must be quite stressed
with Mr. Gill's adventure.

1429
01:23:45.625 --> 01:23:47.792
But this stress is not good
for your child.

1430
01:23:47.875 --> 01:23:49.792
I'm not stressed at all.

1431
01:23:50.000 --> 01:23:52.167
Ever since I've married Mr. Gill,

1432
01:23:52.917 --> 01:23:55.375
I know that Coal India is his family.

1433
01:23:55.875 --> 01:23:56.875
Just like me.

1434
01:23:57.375 --> 01:24:01.458
And whenever there's stress in the family,

1435
01:24:02.250 --> 01:24:04.050
Mr. Gill will be the
first one to reach there.

1436
01:24:04.292 --> 01:24:06.417
This must be the biggest
cultural shock for you.

1437
01:24:06.792 --> 01:24:08.667
You were born and brought up in London.

1438
01:24:08.833 --> 01:24:10.768
And your first delivery
will be done here in Raniganj.

1439
01:24:10.792 --> 01:24:12.542
Yes, but…

1440
01:24:13.042 --> 01:24:14.917
What wasn't there in England

1441
01:24:15.583 --> 01:24:18.542
that you found here
in a Raniganj coal mine?

1442
01:24:18.792 --> 01:24:19.792
Mr. Gill.

1443
01:24:22.042 --> 01:24:24.250
There you go. It's him.

1444
01:24:24.542 --> 01:24:25.875
What did the doctor say?

1445
01:24:25.958 --> 01:24:28.167
She asked me to tell you

1446
01:24:28.250 --> 01:24:31.708
that your wife can get spoilt
if you care for her too much.

1447
01:24:31.958 --> 01:24:32.958
Oh, really?

1448
01:24:33.583 --> 01:24:35.375
Any changes in the medication?

1449
01:24:35.542 --> 01:24:36.542
No.

1450
01:24:36.833 --> 01:24:38.208
- Mr. Gill.
- Yes.

1451
01:24:38.500 --> 01:24:40.208
Are your miners alright?

1452
01:24:40.417 --> 01:24:41.833
Yes, all good.

1453
01:24:54.042 --> 01:24:55.042
NINE

1454
01:24:56.833 --> 01:24:59.375
There's neither water nor gas.

1455
01:24:59.875 --> 01:25:01.167
Rascal!

1456
01:25:04.375 --> 01:25:05.750
- Rascal!
- Bhola!

1457
01:25:05.833 --> 01:25:07.167
- Stop it!
- What happened?

1458
01:25:07.250 --> 01:25:09.167
- I will kill you.
- Why are you hitting him?

1459
01:25:09.375 --> 01:25:11.708
He betrayed us! I won't spare him!

1460
01:25:11.833 --> 01:25:13.875
- Let me go!
- Have you lost your mind?

1461
01:25:14.042 --> 01:25:16.417
He's hand in glove with the management.

1462
01:25:16.500 --> 01:25:17.833
He has lied to us.

1463
01:25:18.083 --> 01:25:20.125
I've seen it myself.

1464
01:25:20.250 --> 01:25:23.542
There is gas forming in the mine.
And it is carbon dioxide.

1465
01:25:23.625 --> 01:25:28.792
- Gas?
- All of us are going to die in here!

1466
01:25:30.667 --> 01:25:32.125
Stop crying.

1467
01:25:32.333 --> 01:25:37.042
Now, it's time to attack the management!

1468
01:25:37.125 --> 01:25:38.125
Bhola is right.

1469
01:25:38.208 --> 01:25:39.250
What do we do now?

1470
01:25:39.333 --> 01:25:42.333
- You're right, Bhola.
- Hey! Don't do this, Bhola.

1471
01:25:42.417 --> 01:25:43.417
Shaligram…

1472
01:25:43.458 --> 01:25:44.542
Listen, Pashu!

1473
01:25:44.708 --> 01:25:48.458
- I'm not in my senses right now.
- You're not getting it.

1474
01:25:48.542 --> 01:25:51.417
Get out of my way.
Get lost! You're their man!

1475
01:25:51.500 --> 01:25:53.292
Listen, Bhola. Listen.

1476
01:25:55.750 --> 01:25:57.125
- Hello.
- This is Bhola.

1477
01:25:57.208 --> 01:26:00.208
We know that there is gas forming here.

1478
01:26:00.417 --> 01:26:02.958
- I want to talk to sir.
- No, it's nothing like that.

1479
01:26:03.042 --> 01:26:05.625
- Have you lost it?
- I want to talk to sir.

1480
01:26:06.167 --> 01:26:08.542
Management is trying to rescue us.
Why are you...

1481
01:26:08.625 --> 01:26:09.875
Shut up, Shaligram.

1482
01:26:09.958 --> 01:26:12.667
Stop defending the management.

1483
01:26:12.958 --> 01:26:15.292
- Leave it. Leave it.
- Get away.

1484
01:26:15.375 --> 01:26:16.375
Puppet.

1485
01:26:16.458 --> 01:26:17.458
Stay away from me.

1486
01:26:17.542 --> 01:26:19.417
You bloody…

1487
01:26:20.208 --> 01:26:21.292
Have you lost it?

1488
01:26:21.625 --> 01:26:23.226
- Why would you raise your hand?
- This is bad.

1489
01:26:23.250 --> 01:26:25.125
- You insulted Bhola.
- Are you alright, Pashu?

1490
01:26:25.208 --> 01:26:26.250
- Yeah.
- Get up.

1491
01:26:26.333 --> 01:26:27.500
How dare you push me?

1492
01:26:28.208 --> 01:26:31.542
- Hey, Shaligram!
- Bhola, you've lost it!

1493
01:26:32.000 --> 01:26:33.583
You're worthless!

1494
01:26:33.667 --> 01:26:35.083
- You idiot!
- Get the first aid kit.

1495
01:26:36.000 --> 01:26:37.000
Kasim!

1496
01:26:40.250 --> 01:26:41.125
Sir!

1497
01:26:41.208 --> 01:26:42.684
Miners have found out
about the gas formation.

1498
01:26:42.708 --> 01:26:43.708
What?

1499
01:26:50.625 --> 01:26:51.745
Gill sir is coming this way.

1500
01:26:51.958 --> 01:26:52.833
- Hello, sir.
- Easy.

1501
01:26:52.917 --> 01:26:55.157
- I've received a complaint from the mine.
- What happened?

1502
01:26:55.208 --> 01:26:57.375
That you all are not
sending them yummy food.

1503
01:26:57.458 --> 01:26:58.542
- Really?
- What's all this?

1504
01:26:59.083 --> 01:27:00.750
The doctor warned us
not to send anything.

1505
01:27:00.833 --> 01:27:02.794
I've convinced the doctor
and he has no objection.

1506
01:27:02.875 --> 01:27:05.792
- Really, sir?
- You all go home and cook yummy food.

1507
01:27:05.875 --> 01:27:06.750
- Yes, let's go.
- Come on.

1508
01:27:06.833 --> 01:27:09.208
- I'll get sweets. You should have some.
- Of course.

1509
01:27:09.667 --> 01:27:11.083
I'll make <i>kachoris</i>.

1510
01:27:19.167 --> 01:27:21.042
- How are you all?
- What is this?

1511
01:27:21.125 --> 01:27:22.208
What's going on?

1512
01:27:25.250 --> 01:27:27.083
My name is Jaswant Singh Gill.

1513
01:27:27.167 --> 01:27:29.000
I'm also a Markatta, just like you.

1514
01:27:29.250 --> 01:27:31.000
Can you hear me?

1515
01:27:32.417 --> 01:27:34.125
Yes, sir. Loud and clear.

1516
01:27:34.583 --> 01:27:35.417
Yes, sir.

1517
01:27:35.500 --> 01:27:39.708
Listen, you all
will have to be a little brave

1518
01:27:40.250 --> 01:27:43.500
so that we can find you
and reunite you with your loved ones.

1519
01:27:44.792 --> 01:27:47.792
Here comes one more puppet
of management.

1520
01:27:48.792 --> 01:27:51.708
Telling us false stories. Idiot.

1521
01:27:51.792 --> 01:27:53.667
Bhola and all the other miners,
listen to this.

1522
01:27:53.875 --> 01:27:54.708
Get lost!

1523
01:27:54.792 --> 01:27:58.333
Pashu lied to you on my instructions.

1524
01:28:00.917 --> 01:28:03.667
If you were made aware
of the gas formation,

1525
01:28:03.750 --> 01:28:06.792
you would have been puffed
up with tension by now.

1526
01:28:06.875 --> 01:28:09.500
I'm sure you know that only buns puff up,

1527
01:28:09.583 --> 01:28:12.292
and taste delicious
if served with pudding.

1528
01:28:12.417 --> 01:28:14.333
But not the miners' faces.

1529
01:28:15.958 --> 01:28:17.083
He talks too much.

1530
01:28:18.958 --> 01:28:19.958
Am I right?

1531
01:28:22.458 --> 01:28:25.500
Look, we need your help.

1532
01:28:25.583 --> 01:28:27.958
So that we can rescue you safely.

1533
01:28:28.500 --> 01:28:32.583
You all have to help each other
to lift each other's spirits.

1534
01:28:32.958 --> 01:28:36.167
Entire Coal India needs your help

1535
01:28:36.250 --> 01:28:37.917
so that the company doesn't shut down.

1536
01:28:39.417 --> 01:28:40.417
Tell me.

1537
01:28:40.500 --> 01:28:42.250
Will you help us?

1538
01:28:43.125 --> 01:28:46.042
Yes, sir.
We will definitely help everybody.

1539
01:28:46.125 --> 01:28:49.208
Yes, sir. We will definitely help you.

1540
01:28:49.292 --> 01:28:51.958
- Yes, sir. We will help you.
- Yes.

1541
01:28:52.625 --> 01:28:54.375
Salute to Coal India!

1542
01:28:54.458 --> 01:28:56.000
- Salute!
- Salute!

1543
01:28:56.083 --> 01:28:59.583
- Salute to Coal India!
- Salute to Coal India!

1544
01:28:59.667 --> 01:29:01.875
- Sir, listen.
- Salute to Coal India!

1545
01:29:01.958 --> 01:29:04.792
- Salute to Coal India!
- Salute to Coal India!

1546
01:29:04.958 --> 01:29:06.583
Salute to Coal India!

1547
01:29:06.667 --> 01:29:08.292
Salute!

1548
01:29:08.500 --> 01:29:10.375
Salute to Coal India!

1549
01:29:12.708 --> 01:29:13.708
How is Nirdosh?

1550
01:29:13.792 --> 01:29:15.250
Both the babies are fine, sir.

1551
01:29:16.958 --> 01:29:20.375
- My wife had sent some sweets for Nirdosh.
- Here you go.

1552
01:29:20.458 --> 01:29:22.226
I thought I would give
it myself and surprise you.

1553
01:29:22.250 --> 01:29:23.684
But God always has some other plans.

1554
01:29:23.708 --> 01:29:24.708
Doesn't matter, sir.

1555
01:29:25.333 --> 01:29:26.917
We will celebrate with the same sweets.

1556
01:29:29.125 --> 01:29:30.125
Thanks, Gill.

1557
01:29:30.958 --> 01:29:34.458
I'm so relaxed with your presence.

1558
01:29:34.583 --> 01:29:35.583
Did you send for me, sir?

1559
01:29:35.833 --> 01:29:36.833
Have you sent the food?

1560
01:29:37.000 --> 01:29:38.440
The family members had brought food.

1561
01:29:38.625 --> 01:29:39.708
We've sent it downstairs.

1562
01:29:44.042 --> 01:29:45.042
Bhola?

1563
01:29:47.167 --> 01:29:48.167
Bhola, listen…

1564
01:29:48.750 --> 01:29:49.750
Bhola!

1565
01:29:52.875 --> 01:29:53.875
Bhola!

1566
01:29:55.000 --> 01:29:56.000
Here.

1567
01:29:56.833 --> 01:29:57.833
Eat this.

1568
01:29:58.083 --> 01:30:00.208
- I don't want it.
- Come on, Bhola.

1569
01:30:00.292 --> 01:30:03.375
The gas will not stop
if you remain hungry.

1570
01:30:04.500 --> 01:30:06.458
Neither will you receive any medal.

1571
01:30:06.542 --> 01:30:08.583
You will receive a medal, in fact.

1572
01:30:08.917 --> 01:30:10.833
You brought us here and trapped all of us.

1573
01:30:10.917 --> 01:30:12.500
- Listen.
- Don't touch me.

1574
01:30:13.000 --> 01:30:14.375
Stay away! Don't come close to me!

1575
01:30:14.833 --> 01:30:16.208
Get lost, idiot!

1576
01:30:17.000 --> 01:30:21.292
I have known you since you were born.

1577
01:30:22.583 --> 01:30:25.625
I also know that you're short-tempered.

1578
01:30:25.750 --> 01:30:28.500
And fainthearted as well.

1579
01:30:28.958 --> 01:30:30.375
Hey, Bhola.

1580
01:30:30.583 --> 01:30:32.625
Stop acting angry now.

1581
01:30:32.708 --> 01:30:33.708
Am I acting?

1582
01:30:33.917 --> 01:30:35.000
Am I acting?

1583
01:30:35.417 --> 01:30:36.542
Shall I dance for you?

1584
01:30:36.667 --> 01:30:38.500
Shall I show you my true colors?

1585
01:30:38.625 --> 01:30:39.958
Oh, Behra…

1586
01:30:40.375 --> 01:30:42.583
You've already made me bleed.

1587
01:30:43.458 --> 01:30:45.583
If you really wish to kill me…

1588
01:30:46.458 --> 01:30:49.208
Then… here you go.

1589
01:30:49.875 --> 01:30:52.417
Take this stone and hit me hard.

1590
01:30:52.583 --> 01:30:53.500
Don't think.

1591
01:30:53.583 --> 01:30:56.167
- Hit me and make me bleed all the more.
- You.

1592
01:31:05.458 --> 01:31:06.667
What happened, Bhola?

1593
01:31:09.125 --> 01:31:13.250
Enough, stop crying now.

1594
01:31:13.667 --> 01:31:15.375
I don't like to see you in tears.

1595
01:31:15.500 --> 01:31:17.458
No, don't cry.

1596
01:31:17.583 --> 01:31:19.333
No, Bhola, don't cry.

1597
01:31:20.125 --> 01:31:21.208
Don't cry.

1598
01:31:21.458 --> 01:31:22.917
Come on, eat something.

1599
01:31:23.250 --> 01:31:24.625
Don't cry.

1600
01:31:24.708 --> 01:31:27.167
See this.

1601
01:31:27.792 --> 01:31:29.667
See what your dad has sent for you.

1602
01:31:30.125 --> 01:31:31.958
Take this.

1603
01:31:32.292 --> 01:31:33.208
Eat.

1604
01:31:33.292 --> 01:31:34.292
I don't want to eat.

1605
01:31:34.792 --> 01:31:35.792
Why?

1606
01:31:36.125 --> 01:31:40.042
All of them got sweets
and other delicacies from their family.

1607
01:31:40.625 --> 01:31:42.708
And look at what my dad has sent for me.

1608
01:31:43.208 --> 01:31:44.208
This bottle gourd?

1609
01:31:45.250 --> 01:31:46.250
I don't want to eat.

1610
01:31:47.375 --> 01:31:48.375
Bottle gourd?

1611
01:31:49.333 --> 01:31:51.542
- Look at him.
- He is incorrigible.

1612
01:31:51.625 --> 01:31:53.000
What made you laugh now?

1613
01:31:55.042 --> 01:31:56.458
I am right.

1614
01:31:56.792 --> 01:31:57.792
Come here.

1615
01:31:57.917 --> 01:32:01.458
Forgive me. I lost my cool.

1616
01:32:09.500 --> 01:32:10.875
Gill, the capsule is ready.

1617
01:32:11.042 --> 01:32:12.250
Get it immediately.

1618
01:32:12.458 --> 01:32:14.179
- What is that?
- Mother, what is this rocket?

1619
01:32:26.917 --> 01:32:27.917
This way, sir.

1620
01:32:30.958 --> 01:32:31.958
See this, Dayal sir.

1621
01:32:34.000 --> 01:32:35.417
A new discovery by Einstein.

1622
01:32:35.917 --> 01:32:37.125
A bird's nest.

1623
01:32:37.875 --> 01:32:39.625
- And then we'll…
- Sir. sir.

1624
01:32:39.750 --> 01:32:42.250
The gas has reached pillar number 15.

1625
01:32:44.750 --> 01:32:45.750
You go.

1626
01:32:45.958 --> 01:32:46.958
Sen sir.

1627
01:32:48.292 --> 01:32:49.958
Your crane is required urgently.

1628
01:32:50.292 --> 01:32:52.000
- My crane.
- Sen.

1629
01:32:53.792 --> 01:32:54.958
Actually, it is…

1630
01:32:55.167 --> 01:32:56.167
Didn't you tell him?

1631
01:32:56.333 --> 01:32:57.694
I told you to pass on the message.

1632
01:32:57.750 --> 01:32:59.708
Sir, it slipped my mind.

1633
01:32:59.792 --> 01:33:01.250
How can you be so irresponsible?

1634
01:33:01.333 --> 01:33:02.542
- What's the matter?
- Hurry up.

1635
01:33:02.625 --> 01:33:04.792
- I'm on it, sir.
- Use this one.

1636
01:33:04.875 --> 01:33:06.542
Upadhyay, come here!

1637
01:33:07.500 --> 01:33:08.875
- Sir!
- What happened?

1638
01:33:09.250 --> 01:33:10.570
I've dismantled the entire crane.

1639
01:33:10.625 --> 01:33:12.375
But I couldn't find the fault.

1640
01:33:12.833 --> 01:33:14.101
It was working properly until yesterday.

1641
01:33:14.125 --> 01:33:17.708
Upadhyay,
if anything happens to our miners,

1642
01:33:17.792 --> 01:33:19.458
you will have to take the responsibility.

1643
01:33:19.958 --> 01:33:21.417
- Get lost.
- I'll fix this, sir.

1644
01:33:22.542 --> 01:33:25.542
Ujjwal sir, I am… I am really
sorry for this blunder.

1645
01:33:25.625 --> 01:33:28.250
Sen!
We are already under pressure.

1646
01:33:28.417 --> 01:33:31.667
Please, don't complicate
this rescue operation more.

1647
01:33:32.750 --> 01:33:36.417
- I beg you.
- Sir, why beg me? This is my duty.

1648
01:33:36.583 --> 01:33:39.625
I am completely on board with the mission.
See, sir.

1649
01:33:39.708 --> 01:33:42.917
- It's the miner's bad luck, not my fault.
- So should I stop the rescue mission?

1650
01:33:43.750 --> 01:33:45.292
I know why you're doing this.

1651
01:33:45.458 --> 01:33:46.333
Why?

1652
01:33:46.417 --> 01:33:51.125
Don't you care about the miners
that are stuck inside?

1653
01:33:51.208 --> 01:33:55.125
Will you stoop so low to fulfill
your personal agenda?

1654
01:33:55.333 --> 01:33:56.958
I had never thought of this.

1655
01:33:57.167 --> 01:33:59.500
You're a shame to Coal India. Shame.

1656
01:33:59.708 --> 01:34:01.708
Sir.
Sir, personal agenda, sir?

1657
01:34:02.083 --> 01:34:03.667
It's nothing like that, sir.

1658
01:34:04.583 --> 01:34:06.601
Upadhyay, please repair it quickly.
Don't you get it?

1659
01:34:06.625 --> 01:34:08.125
- Bindal!
- What happened? Talk to me.

1660
01:34:08.750 --> 01:34:11.417
- Try and arrange another crane.
- Okay.

1661
01:34:13.292 --> 01:34:16.167
Sir, calm down,
we will start doing it manually.

1662
01:34:16.250 --> 01:34:17.083
We don't have time.

1663
01:34:17.167 --> 01:34:18.976
We will switch over as
soon as the crane is here.

1664
01:34:19.000 --> 01:34:20.458
Okay. Thanks, Gill.

1665
01:34:25.083 --> 01:34:28.167
- Tell me, Bindal.
- You have a DEMAG marshal crane, right?

1666
01:34:28.250 --> 01:34:29.250
No.

1667
01:34:30.333 --> 01:34:31.875
- He doesn't have it.
- Next, hurry up.

1668
01:34:32.083 --> 01:34:34.542
- Do you have a 12-ton marshal crane?
- No, Bindal,

1669
01:34:40.250 --> 01:34:41.850
Keep lowering it.
Keep going, keep going.

1670
01:34:41.917 --> 01:34:43.958
- A little to the left.
- Right in the center.

1671
01:34:44.167 --> 01:34:45.000
Keep going.

1672
01:34:45.083 --> 01:34:46.625
I was thinking,

1673
01:34:46.958 --> 01:34:48.833
rescuing them manually

1674
01:34:49.292 --> 01:34:50.625
can take 15 to 20 hours.

1675
01:34:50.833 --> 01:34:52.194
We won't be able to save everyone.

1676
01:34:53.125 --> 01:34:54.917
Tell me if it can come here or not.

1677
01:34:56.625 --> 01:34:57.745
Do you have a marshal crane?

1678
01:35:01.333 --> 01:35:03.458
I gave it to PWD, Raipur.

1679
01:35:08.750 --> 01:35:12.375
Tell Pashu to bring all the miners
to the 29-inch borehole.

1680
01:35:13.667 --> 01:35:15.167
Call up Sharma from Jamtara.

1681
01:35:16.833 --> 01:35:18.917
The crane is in Ranchi.
I will send it immediately.

1682
01:35:19.000 --> 01:35:20.518
It will reach you in six to seven hours.

1683
01:35:20.542 --> 01:35:22.518
Tell the driver to get here
without stopping anywhere.

1684
01:35:22.542 --> 01:35:24.942
Tell him to drive in top gear.
Or else it will be a disaster.

1685
01:35:27.625 --> 01:35:28.542
Look up there.

1686
01:35:28.625 --> 01:35:30.333
Why have they dug such a big hole?

1687
01:35:31.042 --> 01:35:31.958
Get out of my way.

1688
01:35:32.042 --> 01:35:34.333
Uncle, how will they pull us through this?

1689
01:35:34.417 --> 01:35:36.292
It seems they will pull us
up by the rope.

1690
01:35:36.417 --> 01:35:37.333
Shut up, idiot.

1691
01:35:37.417 --> 01:35:38.625
If they pull us up by a rope,

1692
01:35:38.708 --> 01:35:40.875
we will get injured colliding
with the sidewalls.

1693
01:35:41.792 --> 01:35:43.312
I'm sure they will insert a staircase.

1694
01:35:44.583 --> 01:35:45.625
- Pashu!
- Yes.

1695
01:35:45.917 --> 01:35:47.208
The water has reached here.

1696
01:35:48.167 --> 01:35:50.792
- That means the gas is also very close.
- Gas?

1697
01:35:51.208 --> 01:35:52.833
- Pashu, what do we do now?
- Oh, God!

1698
01:35:53.083 --> 01:35:55.667
Did they tell you?
How will they pull us up from this hole?

1699
01:35:56.542 --> 01:35:59.250
Will you explain, Gill?
How the miners will fit in the capsule?

1700
01:35:59.500 --> 01:36:01.708
My height is 6 ft. 1 in.

1701
01:36:01.917 --> 01:36:04.750
And my weight is 77 kilos.

1702
01:36:05.417 --> 01:36:06.875
Sir, as per the records.

1703
01:36:07.500 --> 01:36:09.958
Nobody underground is taller
or wider than me.

1704
01:36:10.042 --> 01:36:12.333
For easy breathing,

1705
01:36:12.417 --> 01:36:15.042
and quick removal
of water seeping inside,

1706
01:36:15.125 --> 01:36:21.000
we've made these small holes
on the capsule, if you can notice.

1707
01:36:21.250 --> 01:36:23.667
The door is kept a foot above.

1708
01:36:23.750 --> 01:36:26.125
Because there will be mud below.

1709
01:36:26.500 --> 01:36:30.167
Sir, we will tie a rope
below the capsule.

1710
01:36:30.333 --> 01:36:33.375
By any chance,
if the capsule is stuck in between,

1711
01:36:33.458 --> 01:36:34.708
and we can't pull it up,

1712
01:36:34.792 --> 01:36:37.917
the miners will use the rope
to lower it down.

1713
01:36:38.958 --> 01:36:41.375
Considering the miners' mental state,

1714
01:36:41.458 --> 01:36:43.542
and to avoid any stampede-like situation,

1715
01:36:43.625 --> 01:36:46.583
a rescue officer will go down
and take charge.

1716
01:36:46.667 --> 01:36:48.042
With his guidance,

1717
01:36:48.208 --> 01:36:51.292
he will ensure the safe ascent
of each miner one by one.

1718
01:36:51.583 --> 01:36:52.708
Excellent work, Gill.

1719
01:36:53.750 --> 01:36:55.875
Sir, with your permission,
I'd like to go down.

1720
01:36:56.083 --> 01:36:57.292
Gill, you rest now.

1721
01:36:57.417 --> 01:36:59.000
You haven't slept for so many days.

1722
01:36:59.708 --> 01:37:01.292
You look tired.

1723
01:37:01.958 --> 01:37:02.958
Sir!

1724
01:37:04.542 --> 01:37:08.458
A member of Sen's team
will go down, risking his life.

1725
01:37:09.167 --> 01:37:10.250
Because they are the best.

1726
01:37:10.542 --> 01:37:11.625
These guys.

1727
01:37:12.292 --> 01:37:13.750
- Good. Proceed.
- Sir.

1728
01:37:19.667 --> 01:37:21.467
- Why have they sent this rope?
- Wait a minute.

1729
01:37:22.333 --> 01:37:24.042
Pull it.

1730
01:37:33.375 --> 01:37:34.208
Sir!

1731
01:37:34.292 --> 01:37:35.667
The capsule has been inspected.

1732
01:37:35.875 --> 01:37:37.583
Now the rescue officer can go down.

1733
01:37:38.917 --> 01:37:40.500
One knock means stop.

1734
01:37:41.417 --> 01:37:42.833
Two knocks mean down.

1735
01:37:42.917 --> 01:37:45.750
- And...
- And three knocks mean up.

1736
01:37:46.042 --> 01:37:48.167
What are you teaching him, Gill?

1737
01:37:49.792 --> 01:37:51.792
- You're going to make history tonight.
- Yes.

1738
01:37:52.625 --> 01:37:54.375
Good luck. My Bengal Tiger.

1739
01:37:58.667 --> 01:37:59.667
Roll.

1740
01:38:05.875 --> 01:38:08.184
- Hey… Pashu, see this. It's coming down.
- It's coming down.

1741
01:38:08.208 --> 01:38:09.833
Something is coming down to take us.

1742
01:38:09.917 --> 01:38:10.917
Oh, God.

1743
01:38:28.417 --> 01:38:29.333
Help!

1744
01:38:29.417 --> 01:38:32.042
- Something is wrong.
- Get me out of here!

1745
01:38:32.542 --> 01:38:34.125
- Stop.
- Hey, stop. Stop!

1746
01:38:34.458 --> 01:38:35.500
Pull back

1747
01:38:35.708 --> 01:38:36.708
What happened?

1748
01:38:37.250 --> 01:38:38.750
- Sen!
- Pull up.

1749
01:38:39.083 --> 01:38:40.000
Pull up fast.

1750
01:38:40.083 --> 01:38:41.458
I will die here.

1751
01:38:41.542 --> 01:38:42.726
It's going up. Hold it.
Pull down. Pull down.

1752
01:38:42.750 --> 01:38:43.750
Stop.

1753
01:38:43.833 --> 01:38:45.073
They must be doing a trial run.

1754
01:38:46.625 --> 01:38:47.625
Pull it up, quick.

1755
01:38:47.917 --> 01:38:49.375
Why are they pulling it up?

1756
01:38:51.333 --> 01:38:52.458
What happened? All okay?

1757
01:38:52.542 --> 01:38:54.083
Sengupta?

1758
01:38:54.208 --> 01:38:55.958
I won't go. This is not a capsule.

1759
01:38:56.042 --> 01:38:57.042
It's the well of death.

1760
01:38:57.125 --> 01:38:58.875
Sengupta, why are you so scared?

1761
01:38:58.958 --> 01:39:00.375
You go. Everybody will die.

1762
01:39:00.542 --> 01:39:02.458
First, you all sent me down
in a bucket.

1763
01:39:03.167 --> 01:39:04.542
And now this capsule.

1764
01:39:05.000 --> 01:39:07.042
- This is Sen sir's order.
- Hey, no.

1765
01:39:07.500 --> 01:39:09.708
Sen is a flatterer.

1766
01:39:09.792 --> 01:39:12.875
He went on calling us Bengal tigers
and fooled us.

1767
01:39:13.750 --> 01:39:15.083
Take this. Send Sen instead.

1768
01:39:15.208 --> 01:39:17.000
Hey! Sengupta!

1769
01:39:17.167 --> 01:39:18.333
Sengupta!

1770
01:39:19.292 --> 01:39:20.875
Sir, he's a coward.

1771
01:39:21.208 --> 01:39:22.667
Don't worry, sir.
I have…

1772
01:39:22.958 --> 01:39:25.417
- Roy, another Royal Bengal Tiger…
- Keep this.

1773
01:39:28.542 --> 01:39:30.583
Roy! Roy!

1774
01:39:31.333 --> 01:39:33.208
Sir, even he turned out to be a coward.

1775
01:39:33.292 --> 01:39:34.708
- Now what?
- What's going on?

1776
01:39:38.000 --> 01:39:39.667
What's going on, Pashu?

1777
01:39:39.917 --> 01:39:41.042
- Wait.
- Be patient.

1778
01:39:43.375 --> 01:39:44.292
Did you call me, sir?

1779
01:39:44.375 --> 01:39:47.333
Decide which rescue officer from
your team would go down.

1780
01:39:47.417 --> 01:39:50.375
Sir, according to the DGMS rule book,
five people should go down.

1781
01:39:50.500 --> 01:39:51.583
That too with a stretcher.

1782
01:39:51.792 --> 01:39:53.083
In this capsule...

1783
01:39:53.167 --> 01:39:55.208
Basu, is this the time to quote rules?

1784
01:39:55.292 --> 01:39:56.375
I'm sorry to say, sir.

1785
01:39:56.458 --> 01:39:59.042
But the DGMS rule book says this.

1786
01:40:00.333 --> 01:40:01.417
Nobody will go.

1787
01:40:09.000 --> 01:40:10.750
Sir, I would have surely gone down, sir.

1788
01:40:11.125 --> 01:40:12.875
But I won't fit into this.

1789
01:40:13.333 --> 01:40:14.417
I realize that.

1790
01:40:16.333 --> 01:40:18.375
- Now who will go down?
- Both the officers ran away.

1791
01:40:18.458 --> 01:40:22.333
Sir, the water level is rising
Please, pull us up.

1792
01:40:22.417 --> 01:40:24.000
Who will save us?

1793
01:40:25.417 --> 01:40:26.500
Ujjwal sir.

1794
01:40:26.958 --> 01:40:28.458
We can't waste time.

1795
01:40:28.958 --> 01:40:30.375
I want to go down.

1796
01:40:31.083 --> 01:40:33.208
- You can
- No, we can't be so selfish, sir.

1797
01:40:33.292 --> 01:40:35.000
Gill has a bright future.

1798
01:40:35.292 --> 01:40:39.833
We can't send a talented officer down
and sacrifice his life.

1799
01:40:39.917 --> 01:40:41.197
Thank you for your concern, sir.

1800
01:40:41.458 --> 01:40:42.458
But I promise you,

1801
01:40:43.000 --> 01:40:45.208
I will have my morning tea with you.

1802
01:40:45.833 --> 01:40:46.833
Okay?

1803
01:41:00.625 --> 01:41:02.583
Oh, Guru Nanak!
Oh, supreme soul!

1804
01:41:03.917 --> 01:41:06.000
Today marks a day of trial

1805
01:41:06.667 --> 01:41:07.792
for your humble Sikh.

1806
01:41:08.292 --> 01:41:09.958
And on this day of trial,

1807
01:41:10.917 --> 01:41:12.625
I earnestly desire Your presence…

1808
01:41:13.417 --> 01:41:15.250
blessings…

1809
01:41:15.750 --> 01:41:17.708
and empowerment to triumph.

1810
01:41:17.958 --> 01:41:19.833
If in my efforts to aid the vulnerable,

1811
01:41:21.000 --> 01:41:23.292
I were to lose my life,

1812
01:41:24.000 --> 01:41:26.125
grant me a place at your sacred feet.

1813
01:41:27.583 --> 01:41:29.125
My soul belongs to You, God.

1814
01:41:29.833 --> 01:41:31.234
All my triumphs also belong to You.

1815
01:41:35.833 --> 01:41:38.167
Gill, anything can happen down there,

1816
01:41:38.250 --> 01:41:39.559
until the crane doesn't reach here.

1817
01:41:39.583 --> 01:41:41.708
Think again, my friend.

1818
01:41:42.750 --> 01:41:43.750
I've thought about it.

1819
01:41:45.042 --> 01:41:46.125
I am going down.

1820
01:41:47.917 --> 01:41:48.917
Take care.

1821
01:42:01.333 --> 01:42:02.333
Be careful.

1822
01:42:04.500 --> 01:42:06.250
Oh, Goddess! Please protect Gill sir.

1823
01:42:06.333 --> 01:42:07.333
Give it here.

1824
01:42:19.875 --> 01:42:20.917
Roll.

1825
01:42:24.083 --> 01:42:25.750
Hey, the rope's coming down.

1826
01:42:26.792 --> 01:42:27.833
Goddess Durga!

1827
01:42:47.250 --> 01:42:48.875
Grab it.

1828
01:42:52.250 --> 01:42:53.250
Grab it. Stop it.

1829
01:42:53.833 --> 01:42:54.833
Mr. Gill!

1830
01:42:58.417 --> 01:43:00.375
Stop it. Pull.

1831
01:43:03.375 --> 01:43:05.458
- What happened?
- Stop it.

1832
01:43:07.125 --> 01:43:08.208
Pull it back.

1833
01:43:11.292 --> 01:43:12.167
Keep watching, sir.

1834
01:43:12.292 --> 01:43:14.250
The nest and the bird,

1835
01:43:14.333 --> 01:43:16.083
both won't reach down, sir.

1836
01:43:23.417 --> 01:43:24.708
- Step back.
- Don't be scared.

1837
01:43:25.417 --> 01:43:28.167
Get the hammer, quick. Hurry up!

1838
01:43:28.292 --> 01:43:29.667
Lock it in place.

1839
01:43:30.167 --> 01:43:31.333
Hurry up.

1840
01:43:31.458 --> 01:43:32.458
Lock it.

1841
01:43:33.708 --> 01:43:36.208
Hammer it down. Do it.

1842
01:43:37.208 --> 01:43:39.875
- Harder. Hit harder.
- Hold on.

1843
01:43:40.917 --> 01:43:42.458
It's locked in place.

1844
01:43:46.667 --> 01:43:47.833
Roll!

1845
01:43:49.458 --> 01:43:50.458
Oh, God!

1846
01:43:50.500 --> 01:43:52.625
Glory to Goddess Earth!

1847
01:43:52.708 --> 01:43:53.788
Keep rolling. Keep rolling.

1848
01:43:54.750 --> 01:43:56.208
It's coming down again.

1849
01:43:57.208 --> 01:43:58.208
What is this?

1850
01:43:58.750 --> 01:43:59.833
What's that box?

1851
01:44:00.167 --> 01:44:01.750
You said a staircase will come down.

1852
01:44:01.833 --> 01:44:03.684
- What kind of device is this?
- Is someone in there?

1853
01:44:03.708 --> 01:44:04.625
Hold it.

1854
01:44:04.708 --> 01:44:05.875
Is someone in there?

1855
01:44:05.958 --> 01:44:07.083
Be careful.

1856
01:44:07.583 --> 01:44:10.708
- Glory to…
- Lord Bajrangbali!

1857
01:44:30.292 --> 01:44:32.125
Sir! Who are you?

1858
01:44:32.375 --> 01:44:34.375
Are you from the military, sir?

1859
01:44:34.458 --> 01:44:36.333
Has the government sent you?

1860
01:44:36.417 --> 01:44:38.208
I'm sure Govardhan sir has sent you.

1861
01:44:38.333 --> 01:44:39.333
Just a minute.

1862
01:44:40.167 --> 01:44:41.417
Where have you come from, sir?

1863
01:44:41.708 --> 01:44:44.083
- Tell us, sir.
- Say something, sir.

1864
01:44:44.375 --> 01:44:45.417
I've come from above.

1865
01:44:45.792 --> 01:44:47.432
I heard you all are having a picnic here.

1866
01:44:47.708 --> 01:44:50.417
So I thought of joining you all.

1867
01:44:50.500 --> 01:44:51.667
He's so funny.

1868
01:44:52.708 --> 01:44:55.208
- Who's Pashu here?
- That's me, sir.

1869
01:44:56.250 --> 01:44:57.250
Well done.

1870
01:44:57.875 --> 01:45:00.208
Sir, see, the water has reached here.

1871
01:45:00.458 --> 01:45:01.684
Will we be able to go out from here?

1872
01:45:01.708 --> 01:45:04.083
Will we be rescued safely, sir?

1873
01:45:04.250 --> 01:45:06.208
- Please, tell us.
- Please, tell us, sir.

1874
01:45:06.292 --> 01:45:07.625
Who can stop you?

1875
01:45:07.708 --> 01:45:10.375
Within a few hours,
you will be with your family.

1876
01:45:10.542 --> 01:45:11.375
- Okay?
- Really, sir?

1877
01:45:11.500 --> 01:45:13.833
Glory to Goddess Kali!

1878
01:45:13.917 --> 01:45:16.667
Glory to Goddess Kali!

1879
01:45:16.750 --> 01:45:19.875
Whoever is injured the most,
will go first.

1880
01:45:19.958 --> 01:45:21.417
- That…
- Sir.

1881
01:45:21.500 --> 01:45:23.917
- Tell me.
- Shaligram.

1882
01:45:24.000 --> 01:45:25.333
He took Shaligram's name.

1883
01:45:25.417 --> 01:45:28.250
See, his leg is badly injured.

1884
01:45:28.333 --> 01:45:29.500
It's starting to rot now.

1885
01:45:29.583 --> 01:45:31.625
- No, not me…
- Send him first.

1886
01:45:31.708 --> 01:45:33.875
Listen to me, sir. Behra should…

1887
01:45:34.250 --> 01:45:35.417
Come on.

1888
01:45:37.625 --> 01:45:38.708
Sir.

1889
01:45:40.167 --> 01:45:41.958
- You're God!
- Hey!

1890
01:45:42.458 --> 01:45:43.500
Now, quickly go inside.

1891
01:45:43.583 --> 01:45:45.833
Otherwise, you will meet God in person.
Go now.

1892
01:45:46.083 --> 01:45:47.417
Careful. Be careful.

1893
01:45:47.500 --> 01:45:49.500
Hurry up, Shaligram. Hurry up.

1894
01:45:49.583 --> 01:45:51.333
See you up there.

1895
01:45:51.417 --> 01:45:52.497
Don't be scared, Shaligram.

1896
01:45:57.042 --> 01:45:58.042
Pull up.

1897
01:46:22.833 --> 01:46:23.833
Oh, God.

1898
01:46:28.250 --> 01:46:31.167
- Glory to…
- Mother Earth!

1899
01:46:32.042 --> 01:46:33.417
Glory to Goddess Kali!

1900
01:46:33.500 --> 01:46:35.375
Glory to Goddess Kali!

1901
01:46:35.667 --> 01:46:38.125
- Glory to…
- Mother Earth!

1902
01:46:38.583 --> 01:46:40.917
Glory to the Goddess Kali!

1903
01:46:41.042 --> 01:46:43.125
Sir, the gas has reached
pillar number 20.

1904
01:46:45.625 --> 01:46:47.417
Glory to Goddess Kali!

1905
01:46:47.500 --> 01:46:49.250
Glory to Goddess Kali!

1906
01:46:49.333 --> 01:46:51.125
Glory to Goddess Kali!

1907
01:46:53.000 --> 01:46:54.875
- Easy. Come on.
- Glory to…

1908
01:46:55.000 --> 01:46:56.208
Mother Earth!

1909
01:46:57.083 --> 01:46:58.917
- Take him.
- Glory to Goddess Kali!

1910
01:46:59.125 --> 01:47:00.500
Glory to Goddess Kali!

1911
01:47:00.750 --> 01:47:02.458
My baby!

1912
01:47:10.875 --> 01:47:11.875
Durga…

1913
01:47:26.375 --> 01:47:29.250
Ujjwal, how much time does it take for
the capsule to come up?

1914
01:47:29.375 --> 01:47:30.500
Fourteen minutes.

1915
01:47:31.417 --> 01:47:32.250
Sharma.

1916
01:47:32.333 --> 01:47:34.375
Don't worry, Bindal.
The crane is on its way.

1917
01:47:39.750 --> 01:47:42.625
Sir, I've three small children.

1918
01:47:42.708 --> 01:47:44.458
Please, send me now.

1919
01:47:44.542 --> 01:47:45.625
Hey, move…

1920
01:47:45.792 --> 01:47:48.542
He's lying, sir.
He has no children.

1921
01:47:48.625 --> 01:47:50.042
I will go next.

1922
01:47:50.125 --> 01:47:51.851
Because I have a direct connection
with Govardhan sir.

1923
01:47:51.875 --> 01:47:53.375
Sir, get me out of this place.

1924
01:47:53.500 --> 01:47:55.875
I don't want to die, sir.
The water level is rising quickly!

1925
01:47:55.958 --> 01:47:58.125
- I want to go next!
- I want to go next!

1926
01:47:58.208 --> 01:48:03.417
- Stop it. Step back.
- I want to go next!

1927
01:48:03.542 --> 01:48:04.792
Quiet!

1928
01:48:05.542 --> 01:48:06.833
Quiet, everyone!

1929
01:48:07.417 --> 01:48:09.458
Quiet!
Be quiet!

1930
01:48:10.542 --> 01:48:11.708
All of you, be quiet!

1931
01:48:12.667 --> 01:48:14.833
Do as I say.

1932
01:48:15.125 --> 01:48:16.375
Nobody will say a word.

1933
01:48:16.625 --> 01:48:18.583
- Okay?
- Yes.

1934
01:48:19.250 --> 01:48:21.167
- Okay?
- Yes, as you say.

1935
01:48:23.708 --> 01:48:26.292
Each of you,
pick up a chit for yourself.

1936
01:48:26.667 --> 01:48:29.792
According to the number mentioned
in the chit,

1937
01:48:29.875 --> 01:48:31.125
you will be able to go up.
Okay?

1938
01:48:31.292 --> 01:48:32.667
No fighting.

1939
01:48:32.750 --> 01:48:34.125
Come one by one,

1940
01:48:34.208 --> 01:48:35.875
and draw a chit. You first.

1941
01:48:41.625 --> 01:48:44.042
Come on. You will be fine. Be strong.

1942
01:48:45.250 --> 01:48:46.917
No, don't cry. Come on.

1943
01:48:47.000 --> 01:48:48.208
Okay, take care.

1944
01:48:48.292 --> 01:48:49.500
- Bravo.
- Don't be scared.

1945
01:48:50.333 --> 01:48:51.333
Close the door.

1946
01:48:51.458 --> 01:48:55.542
<i>When we tread together we shall win</i>

1947
01:48:56.333 --> 01:49:00.792
<i>When we walk hand in hand we shall win.</i>

1948
01:49:00.875 --> 01:49:03.708
- Glory to…
- Mother Earth!

1949
01:49:03.792 --> 01:49:06.333
- Glory to Goddess Kali!
- Glory to Goddess Kali!

1950
01:49:06.417 --> 01:49:08.958
- Glory to…
- Mother Earth!

1951
01:49:12.417 --> 01:49:16.542
<i>We will win</i>

1952
01:49:18.417 --> 01:49:22.625
<i>We know will win</i>

1953
01:49:23.708 --> 01:49:26.125
<i>Promise that we will win</i>

1954
01:49:26.250 --> 01:49:30.375
Couldn't you send anything
other than the bottle gourd?

1955
01:49:30.458 --> 01:49:32.958
Come home, I'll feed you meat.

1956
01:49:36.542 --> 01:49:39.625
- Glory to…
- Mother Earth!

1957
01:49:39.792 --> 01:49:41.667
My son!

1958
01:49:42.958 --> 01:49:45.042
They saved us!

1959
01:49:45.125 --> 01:49:47.208
<i>Promise that we will win</i>

1960
01:49:47.292 --> 01:49:50.458
- Glory to Goddess Kali!
- Glory to Goddess Kali!

1961
01:49:50.542 --> 01:49:51.792
Dad!

1962
01:49:52.042 --> 01:49:53.500
My dear!

1963
01:49:55.750 --> 01:50:00.583
<i>Unite with our kin again</i>

1964
01:50:00.750 --> 01:50:05.750
<i>We will overcome every difficulty
Every hurdle</i>

1965
01:50:06.375 --> 01:50:09.042
<i>Promise that we will win</i>

1966
01:50:09.125 --> 01:50:10.792
<i>We will win</i>

1967
01:50:10.875 --> 01:50:13.833
- Are you okay?
- Glory to Goddess Kali!

1968
01:50:14.333 --> 01:50:18.167
Punish me the way you want, sir.

1969
01:50:22.125 --> 01:50:25.917
<i>- When we tread together, we shall win</i>
- Banke!

1970
01:50:26.000 --> 01:50:31.375
- Mom!
<i>- When we walk hand in hand, we shall win</i>

1971
01:50:32.625 --> 01:50:37.167
<i>When we tread together, we shall win</i>

1972
01:50:37.917 --> 01:50:40.792
- Glory to…
- Mother Earth!

1973
01:50:49.000 --> 01:50:51.083
Relax. The crane will be here soon.

1974
01:50:54.375 --> 01:50:58.833
<i>We know will win</i>

1975
01:50:59.125 --> 01:51:05.792
- Come on.
<i>- Unite with our kin again</i>

1976
01:51:06.792 --> 01:51:09.250
This can take hours.
There's a long traffic jam.

1977
01:51:10.167 --> 01:51:11.167
We're stuck.

1978
01:51:11.875 --> 01:51:14.625
Sir… 40 more miners are yet
to be rescued.

1979
01:51:19.875 --> 01:51:21.035
Why isn't the crane here yet?

1980
01:51:22.042 --> 01:51:23.042
Damn it.

1981
01:51:24.750 --> 01:51:27.792
Although successful this rescue
operation will still be a failure.

1982
01:51:28.792 --> 01:51:32.417
I am sure only twenty miners
will be able to come out.

1983
01:51:32.708 --> 01:51:37.125
The other twenty
will get buried along with Mr. Gill.

1984
01:51:44.708 --> 01:51:47.333
Sir, the water level
is rising very quickly.

1985
01:51:49.208 --> 01:51:50.369
Will the crane reach on time?

1986
01:51:51.125 --> 01:51:52.167
What's your number?

1987
01:51:52.375 --> 01:51:53.250
Sixty-four.

1988
01:51:53.375 --> 01:51:54.542
Crane will be here soon.

1989
01:51:55.458 --> 01:51:56.708
Don't give up hope.

1990
01:51:57.500 --> 01:51:58.500
Okay.

1991
01:51:58.750 --> 01:52:01.500
- Glory to…
- Mother Earth!

1992
01:52:01.625 --> 01:52:03.083
- Glory to Goddess Kali!
- Stop.

1993
01:52:03.500 --> 01:52:04.333
Sir.

1994
01:52:04.417 --> 01:52:06.625
Sen! Come, come.

1995
01:52:06.708 --> 01:52:08.375
- Did you send for me, sir?
- Yes.

1996
01:52:08.792 --> 01:52:12.292
Tell me what you will have.
Tea or creamy milk?

1997
01:52:12.375 --> 01:52:17.417
Only after the miners are safely rescued,
will I eat something.

1998
01:52:17.500 --> 01:52:19.458
I've noticed your efforts.

1999
01:52:19.625 --> 01:52:20.625
Thank you, sir.

2000
01:52:20.750 --> 01:52:22.125
Ganguly, get the ropes.

2001
01:52:22.292 --> 01:52:23.542
Right away.

2002
01:52:24.375 --> 01:52:26.750
- Why the rope, sir?
- I want to tie a dog here.

2003
01:52:29.042 --> 01:52:31.125
Sir! Sir!

2004
01:52:31.708 --> 01:52:32.708
What are you doing, sir?

2005
01:52:32.792 --> 01:52:34.917
Due to a nonsense Bengali like you,

2006
01:52:35.000 --> 01:52:36.417
all of Bengal gets a bad name.

2007
01:52:36.583 --> 01:52:38.250
Please, sir. Don't.

2008
01:52:38.375 --> 01:52:40.125
You call your idiot officers

2009
01:52:40.292 --> 01:52:41.792
Bengal Tigers.

2010
01:52:43.875 --> 01:52:45.833
- Sir…
- Bengal Tiger.

2011
01:52:46.875 --> 01:52:48.167
No, sir. No.

2012
01:52:48.458 --> 01:52:50.708
How dare you play politics with my miners?

2013
01:52:51.167 --> 01:52:52.208
Who told you, sir?

2014
01:52:52.292 --> 01:52:56.417
Ganguly told me everything.

2015
01:52:56.583 --> 01:52:58.583
Had you not developed
a fault in the crane,

2016
01:52:59.417 --> 01:53:01.375
Gill would have definitely succeeded.

2017
01:53:01.542 --> 01:53:04.542
Now, even after the success,
he will be proven a failure.

2018
01:53:05.583 --> 01:53:06.583
The thing is…

2019
01:53:06.625 --> 01:53:08.143
Will you tell me the entire truth?
Or do you want more beating?

2020
01:53:08.167 --> 01:53:09.417
No. I will tell you…

2021
01:53:09.500 --> 01:53:10.375
- I…
- I what?

2022
01:53:10.458 --> 01:53:12.000
I removed the hydraulic hose pipe.

2023
01:53:12.083 --> 01:53:14.292
That's why the crane's
winch stopped working.

2024
01:53:14.958 --> 01:53:18.042
And the capsule
cannot be pulled up or down.

2025
01:53:19.292 --> 01:53:20.500
Good God.

2026
01:53:20.833 --> 01:53:22.583
Without the capsule moving up and down,

2027
01:53:23.333 --> 01:53:24.750
how will we rescue the miners?

2028
01:53:24.833 --> 01:53:26.667
- I will…
- Shut up.

2029
01:53:27.167 --> 01:53:31.833
Listen, I want the crane
here within half an hour.

2030
01:53:32.417 --> 01:53:35.125
- Otherwise, I will expose you.
- Yes.

2031
01:53:35.208 --> 01:53:38.375
And make a mockery out of you.

2032
01:53:38.458 --> 01:53:40.542
There will be no need for that, sir.

2033
01:53:43.375 --> 01:53:46.083
Ujjwal, Sen's crane
will be here in some time.

2034
01:53:46.833 --> 01:53:49.250
Don't worry. I'm with you.

2035
01:53:51.333 --> 01:53:52.917
Ganguly! I'm going to get you for this.

2036
01:53:53.167 --> 01:53:55.583
Hey! Get up, all you shirkers!

2037
01:53:55.667 --> 01:53:56.542
Upadhyay!

2038
01:53:56.625 --> 01:53:59.000
Are you paid for sleeping here?

2039
01:53:59.208 --> 01:54:00.417
Quickly assemble the crane.

2040
01:54:00.625 --> 01:54:02.583
- It is needed right now.
- Where?

2041
01:54:02.667 --> 01:54:04.417
Don't ask questions. Start working.

2042
01:54:08.500 --> 01:54:11.625
- Glory to…
- Mother Earth!

2043
01:54:12.125 --> 01:54:14.833
<i>We shall win</i>

2044
01:54:21.833 --> 01:54:23.458
Go, go. Let it roll down.

2045
01:54:23.875 --> 01:54:28.417
Sir, Diwakar told me on the phone
that he has gone down.

2046
01:54:29.458 --> 01:54:31.333
- You, please…
- I am sorry, Nirdosh.

2047
01:54:31.708 --> 01:54:34.500
None of the officers
were ready to go down, so…

2048
01:54:34.583 --> 01:54:37.792
Come on, why do you feel sorry?
Don't say that.

2049
01:54:37.875 --> 01:54:40.667
He's a miner first and then my husband.

2050
01:54:41.417 --> 01:54:44.458
Now, I know why Gill is so fearless.

2051
